[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cad0ba93-8091-533c-a25a-a5d7cfbae973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471269} {:answer/id #uuid "58928286-7dc1-5197-b088-818d869c772e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad0ba93-8091-533c-a25a-a5d7cfbae973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471269} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7842b45-92cd-5a9d-80f0-68486f8068bc" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472140} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1208e82-0729-505c-90d5-2ea36adad969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471271} {:answer/id #uuid "856332bc-5b98-5598-b36e-d06b239ce7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "856332bc-5b98-5598-b36e-d06b239ce7d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471272} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdb1233e-b724-550d-9b84-7a512bda69ea" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b0d93c4-ca3f-54a1-9887-9ce986e0bba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471273} {:answer/id #uuid "86b14e15-bf92-5a92-b243-e5fd660adda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b14e15-bf92-5a92-b243-e5fd660adda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471274} :answer-field/id #uuid "519c14e9-cdb2-5e83-a514-295e0a236ed8" :answer-field/key "$∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f36cab2-ae5b-5390-a225-e9d92c28352a" :question/math-academy-id "q-183554" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{3}<0$ or ${x}^{2}=0$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set ${Z}^{-},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"${x}^{3}<0$\" is the set ${Z}^{-},$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"${x}^{2}=0$\" is $∅.$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={Z}^{-}\\cup ∅={Z}^{-}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}={Z}^{-}.$\n\n- Statement $∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is *not* empty, the statement $∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(x)$ is ${Z}^{-}.$”; $∃x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,P(x).$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822864b0-d4f3-5454-af92-71c3600dc845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471275} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca96f6e-9734-506e-9a01-9c7094e585f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822864b0-d4f3-5454-af92-71c3600dc845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471275} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bdad168-d730-54bd-a2f5-90e6a40c8c4d" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd50b686-9088-5e8e-9480-616099180f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471277} {:answer/id #uuid "08f6ec98-4ea0-5d97-94e5-7fc31474e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08f6ec98-4ea0-5d97-94e5-7fc31474e537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471278} :answer-field/id #uuid "185a34c6-5872-513c-806d-314d0b02664a" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bbc8f4a-60f3-5fff-9e49-e1ecb34e09db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471279} {:answer/id #uuid "9d04b366-0c6a-52bd-b794-28707736ff32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d04b366-0c6a-52bd-b794-28707736ff32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471280} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7e29fa1-6323-54f9-ac16-2c9f9af53123" :answer-field/key "$∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "79e978ef-4c7c-5a72-a1cc-3c8d675edfbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-183559" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}-2=0⇒{x}^{2}\\in N$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$\\sqrt{x}-2=0$\" is the set ${4},$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"${x}^{2}\\in N$\" is $Z∖{0}.$\n\nSince $A⇒B≡¬A∨B,$ the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\overset{―}{{4}}\\cup (Z∖{0})=(Z∖{4})\\cup (Z∖{0})=Z.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$” is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=Z.$\n\n- Statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is *not* empty, the statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$”; $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9d0b4f3-89cc-5718-9b99-3608b198a961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471281} {:answer/id #uuid "37313c70-39b7-5dc9-b3c4-a19acf370901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d0b4f3-89cc-5718-9b99-3608b198a961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471281} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43f4f46-1ff7-5a5f-b67a-a7033ebb99e9" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472146} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e7b892-0684-5b9b-b9b2-a3f62c816e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471283} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ca0b4c-5971-598e-b066-6bedf819e07d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03e7b892-0684-5b9b-b9b2-a3f62c816e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471283} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe01474-e943-5480-b617-9630e94ff1a0" :answer-field/key "The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)$ is $R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a3cdfb-8bb9-54ae-8804-4c4f876ac849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471285} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fce173-02a3-518a-95ef-ae472714bf66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a3cdfb-8bb9-54ae-8804-4c4f876ac849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471285} :answer-field/id #uuid "24f5bbf3-595e-55dd-8c22-bb49db12000e" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44159662-1bf3-5bee-9ce6-75e394e9c1e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-183586" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R$ and $y\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\n$$\n\nfrom option $∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ For all reals $x$ and $y,$ we have $\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R.$ is false since $\\sqrt{2y}\\in R$ is not true for some real $y.$ Say, for $y=-1.$\n\n- Statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)$ is $R.$” is false. For the predicate\n\n$$\nP(x):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\n$$\n\nwe note that $P(x)$ is false for all values $x\\in R.$ For example, \n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{y}\\in R\n$$\n\nis false, since we can take $y=-1.$ Similarly,\n\n$$\nP(2):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{2y}\\in R\n$$\n\nis false, since we can take $y=-2.$ In general, it's sufficient to take $y=-x$ for any value of $x.$\n\n- Statement $∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R.$ is false. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∀\\,x,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)\n$$\n\n \ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in R\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R}_{P(x)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(x)$ is true over the universal set $R.$ But, according to statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,\\sqrt{xy}\\in R\\,)$ is $R.$”, this is not the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f5b8712-0349-5ec9-be84-86313e9383f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453664} {:answer/id #uuid "99222c1c-3a4e-584c-88d0-dc8348b68220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f5b8712-0349-5ec9-be84-86313e9383f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453664} :answer-field/id #uuid "68de867c-02cd-57fa-bd09-3c999d6ea9c8" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x+1=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311c0395-78e4-5af6-9ae4-5e9d6edf2fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453666} {:answer/id #uuid "532515bd-87e1-5e9b-b032-e51385cc6bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "532515bd-87e1-5e9b-b032-e51385cc6bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453667} :answer-field/id #uuid "5da7d4ee-3b45-5d05-bbd5-5970db34cb14" :answer-field/key "The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35033423-0e24-5eb3-ad49-542e49a2f6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453668} {:answer/id #uuid "94aaeb7f-f626-58e9-8908-cbdc37a51c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35033423-0e24-5eb3-ad49-542e49a2f6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453668} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6e46de2-a550-5250-aeda-06a46b9a6b77" :answer-field/key "$∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42d7175e-7275-5d58-9cbb-adf651178f6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183597" :question/problem "Let $x\\in Z$ and $y\\in Z.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\n$$\n\nfrom option $∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0.$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a integer $y$ such that, for every integer $x,$ we have $x+y=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x+1=0.$ is false since $x+1=0$ is not true for some integer $x.$ Say, for $x=1.$\n\n- Statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)$ is $∅.$” is true. The predicate\n\n$$\nP(y):\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\n$$\n\nis false for every value of $y.$ For example,\n\n$$\nP(0):∀\\,x\\in Z,\\,x=0\n$$\n\nis false for any $x\\ne 0.$ In general, it's sufficient to take $x\\ne -y$ for any $y\\in Z.$ Therefore, its truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement $∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0.$ is false. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,y\\in Z,\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃\\,y\\in Z\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0}_{P(y)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(y)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)$ is $∅.$”, this is not the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀x\\in Z,\\,x+y=0\\,)$ is $∅.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6927f03c-aa7a-56ac-8cd0-c036a11aadc9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Value of a Statement Involving Nested Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1cd21af-f2fc-5f66-997a-4e2c91258940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471287} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f18e7d-fdb8-53fe-8f50-eaaac3ed1598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1cd21af-f2fc-5f66-997a-4e2c91258940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471287} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ed5ac1a-9b04-5b9c-be9d-47fe1e8d63d8" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,\\,2y=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472149} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba4a2deb-40ce-5aff-a38b-c2d9900b7006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471289} {:answer/id #uuid "443319b0-9a52-570e-9382-2ad4c166bcd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba4a2deb-40ce-5aff-a38b-c2d9900b7006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471289} :answer-field/id #uuid "e823795e-dd00-51ef-b876-a9f7aa0d9ea5" :answer-field/key "The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbba717-65e5-566d-8fd3-783fb2ce62b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471291} {:answer/id #uuid "abb18620-d583-5cb5-bb83-c3e2a178cf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb18620-d583-5cb5-bb83-c3e2a178cf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471292} :answer-field/id #uuid "a75d0c30-1919-56dd-97c7-3982426fe9c7" :answer-field/key "$∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "391922f6-f189-52a8-9bf4-83a4fbad32e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-183598" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R$ and $y\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\n$$\n\nfrom option $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a real $x$ such that, for every real $y,$ we have $xy=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $∀\\,y\\in R,\\,2y=0.$ is false since $2y=0$ is not true for some real $y.$ Say, for $y=1.$\n\n- Statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)$ is $∅.$” is false.  The predicate\n\n$$\nP(x):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,xy=0\n$$\n\nis true for some $x\\in R.$ For example, \n\n$$\nP(0):\\,∀\\,y\\in R,\\,0\\cdot y=0\n$$\n\nis true. Therefore, its truth set is not empty.\n\n- Statement $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$ is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R\\,(\\,\\underbrace{∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0}_{P(x)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(x)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to statement “The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0\\,)$ is $∅.$”, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀y\\in R,\\,xy=0.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a7fb68-c72a-5e28-abef-c9c14c8731f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471305} {:answer/id #uuid "7d21b609-6f91-5663-ae33-506abb094118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d21b609-6f91-5663-ae33-506abb094118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471306} :answer-field/id #uuid "13da0634-93a4-522e-a9c5-ed03620db5cd" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $x$ in $xy=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8b210b-083a-55dd-9b97-7d0ce1e26364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471307} {:answer/id #uuid "fd233510-4eb3-506c-8a37-8436954cbcf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8b210b-083a-55dd-9b97-7d0ce1e26364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471307} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b458786-6bfd-5503-9728-a374253066de" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $z$ immediately after $∀$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fe7e95-dafd-55e3-a099-2e08519b6b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471309} {:answer/id #uuid "47e244b1-8fbd-5931-8cbe-a1843732e9b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86fe7e95-dafd-55e3-a099-2e08519b6b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471309} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fddddbd-d644-5857-bcfb-d2ac64e0c2e6" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $z$ in $xz>3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e3ef236-7e81-55bf-8f08-564fa1c1ae50" :question/math-academy-id "q-183669" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,{x}y=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}\\in (1,2),\\,x{z}>3\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- The occurrence of $x$ in $xy=1$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- The occurrence of $z$ immediately after $∀$ is *bound* since it is placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,xy=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (1,2),\\,xz>3\\,)\n$$\n\n- The occurrence of $z$ in $xz>3$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∀$ that uses $z:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∃y\\in (0,1),\\,xy=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀z\\in (1,2),\\,\\overbrace{x{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>3}^{\\text{scope of }∀z})\n$$\n\n \n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∃{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}=1\\,)⇒(\\,∀{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (1,2),\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>3\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is “The occurrence of $x$ in $xy=1$” only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a04d1c6-5fef-5eb1-b8a0-6e8d2bc0cb0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471353} {:answer/id #uuid "28dd7535-fa0f-594a-badb-bbba90cf96c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28dd7535-fa0f-594a-badb-bbba90cf96c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471354} :answer-field/id #uuid "39dda0b1-b1e4-5398-90a6-9476fff2abd4" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9546767-c4b3-57a2-b994-f01725c8569f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471355} {:answer/id #uuid "c9abd13e-9f4d-567b-bbf2-70e8c2cc7a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9546767-c4b3-57a2-b994-f01725c8569f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471355} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd300e54-475d-59cb-b72c-6f2553db14b3" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2624e8-195a-5c38-b473-4ece34824be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471357} {:answer/id #uuid "e0091fd0-01af-5579-805f-bdd3dda2655a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e2624e8-195a-5c38-b473-4ece34824be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471357} :answer-field/id #uuid "d218648f-439f-5a95-ad9a-80f155bba199" :answer-field/key "$∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a35352a2-6307-508d-9bf3-f6a84812f3f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-216492" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $2x+1=0$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the solution of the equation $2x+1=0$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ but this solution doesn't belong to the universal set. Therefore, the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=∅.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is true. The truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$” is false.\n\n- Statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$ is false. Since ${T}_{P}$ is empty, the statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "320c4694-1904-5fc7-a324-a4c89f0e3257" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Existential Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/id #uuid "6de9a5a5-ab7e-5d26-821c-9f50ad7ae54d" :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5b5e933-63cd-5870-9ff5-3e6516c2f0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453782} {:answer/id #uuid "2aef0dc4-b15d-5cd2-a2c5-b65739ff18c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5b5e933-63cd-5870-9ff5-3e6516c2f0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453782} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c056c8-efa4-563a-832c-a22f72e55793" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454641} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d20c045d-a7b6-582a-996a-61a2e3b07ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453784} {:answer/id #uuid "8446b446-cf09-5f50-822c-c972a0839ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d20c045d-a7b6-582a-996a-61a2e3b07ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453784} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9caea3-9b43-5d58-88a6-7f613d2c07c6" :answer-field/key "The truth set of $P(x)$ is $R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454642} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8d1138-120f-514c-9737-44ab8207b868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453786} {:answer/id #uuid "1497c774-e9e5-56fc-a33f-16e7810e0f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1497c774-e9e5-56fc-a33f-16e7810e0f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453787} :answer-field/id #uuid "79528333-5062-5700-b901-57ac2078cec1" :answer-field/key "$∃x\\in R,\\,P(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac3fd956-3cf4-5e15-bb4c-d8f2d84edef6" :question/math-academy-id "q-216493" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x<1$ and $|x|\\ge 1.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $R,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that:\n\n- the truth set of \"$x<1$\" is $(-\\infty ,1),$ and\n\n- the truth set of \"$|x|\\ge 1$\" is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the truth set of our predicate is\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,1)\\cap ((-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ))=(-\\infty ,-1].\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$” is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement “The truth set of $P(x)$ is $R.$” is false. Indeed, ${T}_{P}\\ne R.$\n\n- Statement $∃x\\in R,\\,P(x).$ is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is not empty, the statement $∃x\\in R,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∃x\\in R,\\,P(x).$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fda7182c-9b27-54fb-ae1a-8d57fe19c36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471359} {:answer/id #uuid "e32d31ef-16ba-5f7a-a9dd-81cd32b4ec01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fda7182c-9b27-54fb-ae1a-8d57fe19c36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471359} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c2c916d-9df2-5d54-8d54-3148860ec045" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $y$ immediately after $∀$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d776f2f-d7f1-52a2-ab41-69e9765f8907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471361} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1d90a0-d385-5638-a7af-b463cfa7cd50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a1d90a0-d385-5638-a7af-b463cfa7cd50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471362} :answer-field/id #uuid "c52a9fa8-43ce-56c3-ac5e-6c9511f4082a" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $x$ in $y+x\\le z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24da09b9-7a22-5782-afed-5cb9868986bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471363} {:answer/id #uuid "3e03b584-5c34-5bbd-99fe-1e1d25f1324b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e03b584-5c34-5bbd-99fe-1e1d25f1324b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471364} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb6dd46-9d46-5c39-81ef-15638fcdf267" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $z$ on the right side of $y+x\\le z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "390e8909-b67e-5f3a-bb33-1726ba1d68d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-216530" :question/problem "$$\n∀{\\,y}\\in Z,\\,y+{x}\\le {\\,z}\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- The occurrence of $y$ immediately after $∀$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n∀{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,y+x\\le z\n$$\n\n- The occurrence of $x$ in $y+x\\le z$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- The occurrence of $z$ on the right side of $y+x\\le z$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $z.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n∀{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,y+{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\le {z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrences are “The occurrence of $x$ in $y+x\\le z$”; “The occurrence of $z$ on the right side of $y+x\\le z$” only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381874 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "051e28ef-ac7f-5b29-bd93-c1e24a4bc699" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Free and Bound Occurrences of Variables" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050691 :topic/id #uuid "5f607ed3-b581-5e92-9101-c32dd179ab13" :topic/math-academy-id 2792 :topic/title "Nested Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2883b9ba-32bd-5ff5-bcce-b579c830b5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471365} {:answer/id #uuid "555b55f4-34bd-5b0e-9e56-002b7921c1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555b55f4-34bd-5b0e-9e56-002b7921c1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471366} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ba74c19-e05e-599b-bbd8-455461faedc0" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $n$ in $x>n+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e07894ab-f2fd-5837-8dce-530c9db39f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471367} {:answer/id #uuid "8256ae5a-2145-576f-b24c-70fde43e43bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07894ab-f2fd-5837-8dce-530c9db39f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471367} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f394222-c342-5bf2-9565-301ff724543e" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $z$ in ${z}^{3}-1=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c293a14-efb0-5e66-bdb9-90ab3fd059d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471369} {:answer/id #uuid "6b596922-2fca-5d75-b70f-37831468c2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b596922-2fca-5d75-b70f-37831468c2ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471370} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ad30a7-aa49-5946-bf6a-d22d986bc83e" :answer-field/key "The occurrence of $y$ on the right side of ${z}^{3}-1=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d9a12d6-16ca-57db-975d-02505a889530" :question/math-academy-id "q-216618" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∀x\\in N,\\,x>{n}+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃z\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}-1={y}\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- The occurrence of $n$ in $x>n+1$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- The occurrence of $z$ in ${z}^{3}-1=y$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃z$ that uses $z:$ \n\n$$\n(\\,∀x\\in N,\\,x>n+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃z\\in R,\\,\\overbrace{{z}^{3}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}^{\\text{scope of }∃z}\\,)\n$$\n\n- The occurrence of $y$ on the right side of ${z}^{3}-1=y$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $y.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in N,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is “The occurrence of $n$ in $x>n+1$”; “The occurrence of $y$ on the right side of ${z}^{3}-1=y$” only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35db3c9b-02b9-5c7d-a8c1-09176c032e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453934} {:answer/id #uuid "29ce6cf9-27c1-5fd1-8cbf-f6799920b1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29ce6cf9-27c1-5fd1-8cbf-f6799920b1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453935} :answer-field/id #uuid "7acd2660-cd2a-577c-9376-da725e19aef5" :answer-field/key "${f}_{y}(1,-1)$ is defined" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454717} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad87f6c0-0c68-522a-8122-d035dbe64fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453936} {:answer/id #uuid "859d9311-70b2-5685-b197-4a91254e744a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "859d9311-70b2-5685-b197-4a91254e744a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453937} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d1d4321-6803-5056-a842-c68247cc1177" :answer-field/key "Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454718} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2fda6f3-3bce-51e5-9059-f8105ac02f72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453938} {:answer/id #uuid "403cb9a2-360b-5e77-afe9-99e083474952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2fda6f3-3bce-51e5-9059-f8105ac02f72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453938} :answer-field/id #uuid "65daae6a-989b-50a5-b441-759088075f44" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(1,1)$ is defined" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa8a43bb-df08-5eee-88ea-f9abcdd2fb8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72011" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}\\cdot \\frac{-1}{2\\sqrt{x-y}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{x-y}}}{2\\sqrt{x-y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one. \n\n- Statement “${f}_{y}(1,-1)$ is defined” is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,-1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}={e}^{\\sqrt{2}},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,-1)=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{2}}}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,0)$” is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,0)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,0)={e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}={e}^{1}=e,\n$$\n\nand both partial derivatives are also defined at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,0) & =\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}}{2\\sqrt{1-0}}=\\frac{{e}^{1}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{e}{2} \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,0) & =-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-0}}}{2\\sqrt{1-0}}=-\\frac{{e}^{1}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=-\\frac{e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{x}(1,1)$ is defined” is false. If we substitute $(1,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(1,1)=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1-1}}}{2\\sqrt{1-1}}=\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2\\sqrt{0}}=\\frac{1}{0}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“${f}_{y}(1,-1)$ is defined” and “Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,0)$”  only'."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45d1ed56-bfc6-5bda-a5c6-d5385ab5bd77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453940} {:answer/id #uuid "bf41f840-b49c-5384-a274-dfe536fcb33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf41f840-b49c-5384-a274-dfe536fcb33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453941} :answer-field/id #uuid "edafd0ac-42e0-5d4a-be7b-7aa902ffa1b6" :answer-field/key "${f}_{y}(1,1,1)$ is defined" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454720} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060c118c-98d6-5841-94fb-d05d803c937b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453942} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca503bc-9f0b-57b9-9107-116d82172e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "060c118c-98d6-5841-94fb-d05d803c937b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453942} :answer-field/id #uuid "97a453da-0bfb-5722-95ac-96c9ea20e34e" :answer-field/key "${f}_{z}(0,1,2)$ is defined" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8b8bc4-d09b-5051-b032-eb64e490a6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453944} {:answer/id #uuid "5922a222-d689-5f69-94af-6d12b904bec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8b8bc4-d09b-5051-b032-eb64e490a6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453944} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e81b99c-60a0-5dd3-8161-a53cd384fae9" :answer-field/key "The partial derivative with respect to $x$ is defined at $(0,1,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff98942c-b72f-558c-86fd-786f6575a16d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72019" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{2x+y-z}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+y-z}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x+y-z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{y}(1,1,1)$ is defined” is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,1,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,1,1)=\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+1-1}=\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,1,1) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+1-1}}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{z}(0,1,2)$ is defined” is false. If we substitute $(0,1,2)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(0,1,2)=\\sqrt{2\\cdot 0+1-2}=\\sqrt{-1},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since the number under the radical is negative.\n\n- Statement “The partial derivative with respect to $x$ is defined at $(0,1,1)$” is false. If we substitute $(0,1,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(0,1,1)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 0+1-1}}=\\frac{1}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“${f}_{y}(1,1,1)$ is defined” only'." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"} :activity/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445246} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445261}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050207 :topic/id #uuid "36521b0a-e13c-5296-b2d4-078f2470ad6d" :topic/math-academy-id 1992 :topic/title "Double Integrals Over Rectangular Domains"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c1ebce9-eb86-5d86-ac05-3d046c19d154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471507} {:answer/id #uuid "191266bf-17fa-5b3f-a69d-006602f0b1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c1ebce9-eb86-5d86-ac05-3d046c19d154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471507} :answer-field/id #uuid "51a227da-90c2-52f9-9077-b27b96efcf2d" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee27b98a-d403-540e-b4d1-58599c0791ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471509} {:answer/id #uuid "28c28979-9f71-531a-95a5-9727b10ce997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28c28979-9f71-531a-95a5-9727b10ce997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471510} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d0d5f5-af4c-574f-bc3d-7168cd1ab3e6" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfbf44d-eb98-55d5-8c14-3e22b731f235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471511} {:answer/id #uuid "98822c58-2bb2-5161-be03-5dc25f69be74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98822c58-2bb2-5161-be03-5dc25f69be74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471512} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e78bf6a-ca6f-5737-8263-4c7e4e4b8a4d" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d63a269e-ef04-5d49-b4b0-245cf68e9dfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-72167" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $-2$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-1$ to $-1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$; ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049745 :topic/id #uuid "108b7bdf-575a-514c-aeb4-4d6378b3df40" :topic/math-academy-id 2627 :topic/title "Surjections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc5affe6-4770-5548-9507-5c89a64c9b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471561} {:answer/id #uuid "dde18b4b-8640-5ed9-92a5-b12e63fff964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dde18b4b-8640-5ed9-92a5-b12e63fff964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471562} :answer-field/id #uuid "320576ab-882c-5a79-b3a3-b28f006e057e" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472286} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93698920-d848-54df-841c-dab3e524be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471563} {:answer/id #uuid "096b59d8-3cb6-5a1b-b69d-9f2da2407523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93698920-d848-54df-841c-dab3e524be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471563} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b2efca-871f-5c8a-891c-318bab239316" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bb77a49-0313-5979-a239-3449474b79f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471565} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b30ce9-1264-57ec-9dd7-435dcd422034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb77a49-0313-5979-a239-3449474b79f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471565} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2e21158-0876-5654-b53e-3a157ac915f2" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **onto**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8bf28a0-bd57-55ca-8858-3f8b81db61da" :question/math-academy-id "q-80019" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}+1?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/be/bed7b280998fe987276ca5820b987f672404d52d00f532db819db1166118ed70.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$  in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$” is true. From the graph, the lowest $y$-value is $1,$ and it occurs at the point $(2,1).$ The graph will cover all $y$-values from $y=1$ and greater, including the number $1,$ so the range of the function is $[1,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false. Consider $y=0.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **onto**” is false. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The range of $f$ is $[1,\\infty )$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049745 :topic/id #uuid "108b7bdf-575a-514c-aeb4-4d6378b3df40" :topic/math-academy-id 2627 :topic/title "Surjections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "325415a9-4e64-5acc-accc-7937c4f8a651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471573} {:answer/id #uuid "509ead5d-1ed4-51e9-ade5-e20f4dccf244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "509ead5d-1ed4-51e9-ade5-e20f4dccf244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471574} :answer-field/id #uuid "57e14e43-325d-539a-b71c-0daeffea3e8d" :answer-field/key "There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472292} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b751fc1-76b7-5b04-9e99-a6f9345ac7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471575} {:answer/id #uuid "de102440-2957-5573-8f72-f4a754cac936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de102440-2957-5573-8f72-f4a754cac936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471576} :answer-field/id #uuid "0338e231-7e8a-5d9b-ac75-df2b48d71c2c" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472293} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84c47fd5-45fa-5f40-8718-94f6a52adcc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471577} {:answer/id #uuid "67b4ec67-ecda-57e4-bc7d-c948f865ae0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67b4ec67-ecda-57e4-bc7d-c948f865ae0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471578} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ad4eb7-1db6-54bf-bd3e-c94b7169a0f7" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ab13059-2894-50dc-959d-d70d8ebc3fee" :question/math-academy-id "q-80202" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f445040526c9b72e66dd29b15b32a89ec8b47a4cd2ae17bed009948dbce655d.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$  in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=3$” is true. According to the diagram, we have $f(4)=3$ (we have an arrow from $4\\in X$ to $3\\in Y$). So, there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true. As we can see from the diagram, for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is true. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true, $f$ is a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “There exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=3$”; “$∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y$”; “$f$ is a surjection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152132 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fe686b5-c7f0-58e6-9e46-e769a9193b21" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049745 :topic/id #uuid "108b7bdf-575a-514c-aeb4-4d6378b3df40" :topic/math-academy-id 2627 :topic/title "Surjections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d0e910b-07da-5be7-aca5-1464a56adaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471579} {:answer/id #uuid "c45c5006-3ed6-5ac1-8fc1-07a132bcbf7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c45c5006-3ed6-5ac1-8fc1-07a132bcbf7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471580} :answer-field/id #uuid "66af87e4-0aff-5341-adb0-03db5faabc4f" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $[2,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96193f3e-583a-5047-84ce-2a4a9a56fb1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471581} {:answer/id #uuid "f1e35ee5-44a6-5591-90b4-551fc8e0781c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96193f3e-583a-5047-84ce-2a4a9a56fb1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471581} :answer-field/id #uuid "704cd320-5ab7-5fe8-841c-e79a98687dc7" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472296} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a91db0ce-3dd2-5a2a-875c-8e5f53dcb5b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471583} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd0637a-d57e-5887-a7f4-b98353c5d11d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a91db0ce-3dd2-5a2a-875c-8e5f53dcb5b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471583} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd3da033-01b5-56a0-86c7-f2e78645a591" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd4aa8c6-1cff-54d1-b1c7-27592615a44f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80224" :question/problem "![](images/86/86568c2024cfeb7f6605cd43a92f29492e24a1366216f51aa238c8c339bcff59.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $[2,\\infty )$” is true. From the graph, we see that the lowest $y$-value is $y=2,$ and it occurs at the point $(-2,2).$ The graph covers all $y$-values greater than $y=2,$ including $2$ itself.  So, the range of the function is $[2,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false. Consider $y=0.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The range of $f$ is $[2,\\infty )$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049745 :topic/id #uuid "108b7bdf-575a-514c-aeb4-4d6378b3df40" :topic/math-academy-id 2627 :topic/title "Surjections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b64c7222-8178-5745-8e74-7d3d3ada236d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454024} {:answer/id #uuid "e561b55b-0014-50e9-9583-fa8316227227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b64c7222-8178-5745-8e74-7d3d3ada236d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454024} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdf7c354-9699-5c96-81a6-477592bd5789" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $[0,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454762} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed2af1a7-3c28-56d8-928f-ef61266cf553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454026} {:answer/id #uuid "2eed2737-812f-5961-9396-c460b64bbd69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2eed2737-812f-5961-9396-c460b64bbd69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454027} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f44b5c3-35bf-51b2-aaca-38d7b8b70d4f" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf8d5f67-d6d3-51d6-ad2b-8ee69006b10c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454028} {:answer/id #uuid "fc265a77-f3c2-54a8-bb4c-ef3c2eef3d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc265a77-f3c2-54a8-bb4c-ef3c2eef3d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454029} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b10f796-218a-5bcd-aac9-a709584f5702" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **onto**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9c388c8-17e9-5b67-9968-fd45f98197a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-80261" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={x}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function. \n\n![](images/1a/1a2b29a675770d1c8331672656a6054b052ebfebdf6bc61e5bd6459468087215.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $[0,\\infty )$” is false. The graph covers all $y$-values, so the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$, then for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **onto**” is true. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true, $f$ is a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$”; “$f$ is **onto**” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63a2b195-d0b3-580c-9230-58533d86afd5" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Domain and Codomain Is the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049745 :topic/id #uuid "108b7bdf-575a-514c-aeb4-4d6378b3df40" :topic/math-academy-id 2627 :topic/title "Surjections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f01503f6-fc6a-50e4-a24c-82f19ac86d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471585} {:answer/id #uuid "78710886-40f8-5c1b-bb4c-05340d1f4065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f01503f6-fc6a-50e4-a24c-82f19ac86d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471585} :answer-field/id #uuid "07421070-0c5d-5d8f-8e44-348ba4c3999d" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $(-\\infty ,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c20f795e-cec6-5874-8045-861cb92997f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471587} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe98e74-34ab-5964-8833-978e5077d5e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fe98e74-34ab-5964-8833-978e5077d5e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471588} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd145508-9c0f-52b0-b43b-784cd668ecc0" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b8bed7a-4d9f-5851-9351-509a1766f37c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471589} {:answer/id #uuid "a93e5302-d581-5944-905a-6d90e8f750f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a93e5302-d581-5944-905a-6d90e8f750f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471590} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc349d13-47e7-5812-9a17-5ba87b367d65" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12ed8ad0-48d9-538c-959c-ba969b6bfa2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-80262" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e4dd0466c7c98d5cb6dfd0f73cd107636a2df258149778af444f58f36306b326.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $(-\\infty ,1]$” is false. In fact, as the arrows indicate, the graph covers all $y$-values, so the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true. Since the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$, then for all $y$ contained within $R,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is true. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true, $f$ is a surjection of $R$ onto $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" “$∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$” and “$f$ is a surjection” only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1324fd0b-5388-5133-ad6a-72d658e3c903" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049745 :topic/id #uuid "108b7bdf-575a-514c-aeb4-4d6378b3df40" :topic/math-academy-id 2627 :topic/title "Surjections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2725fc60-80d0-516f-b983-0ae212f98868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471591} {:answer/id #uuid "2b531d3c-49a0-5328-a025-2aa8c48cff65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2725fc60-80d0-516f-b983-0ae212f98868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471591} :answer-field/id #uuid "e64a4751-1838-5585-94bd-747b7d1ec789" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $[0,5]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6035af70-8e8b-5c3c-b8b1-367fa3fcec12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471593} {:answer/id #uuid "9b90fe71-9f57-5d16-9093-46d8f32c9d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b90fe71-9f57-5d16-9093-46d8f32c9d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471594} :answer-field/id #uuid "b15de725-2c11-5f82-8d75-f2db75305ea2" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in [0,4],$ $∃\\,x\\in [-1,4]$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "456464aa-ba89-5881-8c5b-164bf9727137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471595} {:answer/id #uuid "64e2ed41-e542-57ba-a448-4892dad3fa12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "456464aa-ba89-5881-8c5b-164bf9727137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471595} :answer-field/id #uuid "b590bb5c-5056-5807-b5ec-196b7c93dba1" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d072f9fe-6a97-527b-a8fc-6dbaa90f64fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-80296" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4ae29c6d6a446a302f4104e339a067a5e43fd82088e773fac7e8e9b70b342f3.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-1,4]\\to [0,5]$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $[0,5]$” is false. From the graph, the highest $y$-value is $4$ and the lowest $y$-value is $0.$ The graph covers all $y$-values between $0$ and $4$, including these numbers, so the range of the function is $[0,4].$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in [0,4],$ $∃\\,x\\in [-1,4]$ such that $f(x)=y$” is true. Since the range of the function is $[0,4]$, it follows that for all $y$ contained within $[0,4],$ there exists some $x$ contained within $[-1,4]$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. Since the range of $f$ is not $[0,5],$ then it's *not true*  that for all $y$ contained within $[0,5],$ there exists some $x$ contained within $[-1,4]$ such that $f(x)=y.$ In conclusion, $f$ is not a surjection of $[-1,4]$ onto $[0,5].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∀\\,y\\in [0,4],$ $∃\\,x\\in [-1,4]$ such that $f(x)=y$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152134 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1324fd0b-5388-5133-ad6a-72d658e3c903" :knowledge-point/title "Functions Whose Codomain Is a Real Interval" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049745 :topic/id #uuid "108b7bdf-575a-514c-aeb4-4d6378b3df40" :topic/math-academy-id 2627 :topic/title "Surjections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "947844cd-1269-59a2-9579-38c3bf5a1be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454030} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b66751-c728-5194-852e-fce7cee82cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7b66751-c728-5194-852e-fce7cee82cdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454031} :answer-field/id #uuid "eee835c5-8b1e-58cf-86a7-d01172af5440" :answer-field/key "The range of $f$ is $[1,8]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454765} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2add6c0f-1b98-5085-885c-4f5943c964ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454032} {:answer/id #uuid "5aeaced6-0274-5f64-9e42-e938b5c58ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2add6c0f-1b98-5085-885c-4f5943c964ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454032} :answer-field/id #uuid "88a19825-3e91-5892-ac06-9e5a82fc51df" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,y\\in [0,8],$ $∃\\,x\\in [0,3]$ such that $f(x)=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66953d10-bfc0-555b-8107-3a6726174100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454034} {:answer/id #uuid "b957c21c-274f-5957-b83e-f42201b11e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66953d10-bfc0-555b-8107-3a6726174100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454034} :answer-field/id #uuid "b28a6f71-cba3-51e4-bc5d-72a067179d3e" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **onto**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5848bc45-4fef-5470-b7b2-022f9067ecb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-80297" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[0,3]\\to [0,8]$ which is given by $y={2}^{x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/47/47407d426cf9bb816c0b3dd052138b637bc73e7aa6d751278b20d8add020526d.png)\n\n \nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection (also known as *onto*) if, for *every* element $y$ in $Y,$ there is *at least one* element in $X$ that maps to $y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The range of $f$ is $[1,8]$” is true. From the graph, the highest $y$-value is $8$ and the lowest $y$-value is $1.$ The graph covers all $y$-values between $1$ and $8$, including these numbers, so the range of the function is indeed $[1,8].$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,y\\in [0,8],$ $∃\\,x\\in [0,3]$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false. Consider, for example,  $y=0.$ As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x\\in [0,3]$ such that $f(x)=0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $[0,8],$ there exists some $x$ contained within $[0,3]$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **onto**” is false. Since statement “$∀\\,y\\in [0,8],$ $∃\\,x\\in [0,3]$ such that $f(x)=y$” is false, $f$ is not a surjection of $[0,3]$ onto $[0,8].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The range of $f$ is $[1,8]$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382400 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152200 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "100ab73e-3dad-5b15-9da2-d244c67bcc9b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049229 :topic/id #uuid "e52ab899-5fcb-50d2-afee-4830a70f16df" :topic/math-academy-id 2616 :topic/title "Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6a14e7a-b747-5daa-a6d8-ddf27bcb3435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454054} {:answer/id #uuid "ef203a18-6200-50a4-8f37-40f6d775a047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6a14e7a-b747-5daa-a6d8-ddf27bcb3435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454054} :answer-field/id #uuid "368e434e-c352-5632-8222-8c74717eb1e3" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{R}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454777} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89d2bcf1-e624-5732-9da9-f26392281661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454056} {:answer/id #uuid "65454c69-ffda-5315-a369-0369fd32aa73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65454c69-ffda-5315-a369-0369fd32aa73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454057} :answer-field/id #uuid "1998fa1f-9db2-528c-8a77-26d7fb35e77f" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a0139cb-9ef6-5b37-92da-cfe05b47fe33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454058} {:answer/id #uuid "03dcd1c2-23f1-50a4-923d-5b396bf94b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03dcd1c2-23f1-50a4-923d-5b396bf94b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454059} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fd599f9-74b2-5a43-9569-f24f6afb0be6" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-3,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47830ab2-2bae-52c6-8c9c-df89a69a6369" :question/math-academy-id "q-80536" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/5c/5c5dbc673c2c6a9bd0a4f06223133e21e2dcbbdbaa2dfe2de2b29d8824dd821e.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement “${∬}_{R}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-2,2]$” is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$ Also, the integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statements “${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$” and “${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-3,3]$” are true. In both cases, the rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$”; “${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-3,3]$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050777 :topic/id #uuid "65e4f73e-43a8-5089-914d-135e7396b995" :topic/math-academy-id 2821 :topic/title "Logical Equivalence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b406b689-3c74-5395-adad-002234ac8699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471657} {:answer/id #uuid "317451ef-f89e-5251-a9e3-a76136ab46fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "317451ef-f89e-5251-a9e3-a76136ab46fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471658} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d48b900-e4e0-5b60-897f-7050febe69c7" :answer-field/key "$¬(¬A∨¬B)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed3c720f-f39d-5b54-8fff-3b1de6263fb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471659} {:answer/id #uuid "341e88e4-f3fe-58f3-8ec1-ebde1c717286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "341e88e4-f3fe-58f3-8ec1-ebde1c717286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471660} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e88922e-58b5-569b-a8b4-fb942b9c3a45" :answer-field/key "$A∧B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec04081c-be9d-57b9-836b-b15362aa3a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471661} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2a1bd1-1966-5f8c-93f4-2ac284a874e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec04081c-be9d-57b9-836b-b15362aa3a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471661} :answer-field/id #uuid "94e63a8b-40e6-5937-baa4-a71931a1c8d8" :answer-field/key "$A∨B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1094e86-e368-5edf-a0b9-d55c19636e6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81485" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(¬A∨¬B)\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ | $\\,A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬(¬A∨¬B)$ and $A∧B$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $¬(¬A∨¬B)$; $A∧B$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157397 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Integrals That Evaluate to Zero" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048495 :topic/id #uuid "a4841cae-d95f-5e07-960c-2030a42a2568" :topic/math-academy-id 2975 :topic/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals Using Symmetry"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d61685a2-df2b-533f-a32e-665b4e611471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471783} {:answer/id #uuid "c3019c91-cb8c-5c1a-9534-292bf0d6875b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d61685a2-df2b-533f-a32e-665b4e611471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471783} :answer-field/id #uuid "672fb52d-9c09-5df4-9340-bbe334fb6578" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-5}^{5}2{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e293b232-16ce-59f4-9d38-5d1277b07288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471785} {:answer/id #uuid "53eb1a4b-765d-5798-903d-c9f22c2a7f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53eb1a4b-765d-5798-903d-c9f22c2a7f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471786} :answer-field/id #uuid "12f3fc33-13ad-5e24-9481-f3353ab88869" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472398} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbb5f7e3-e049-5251-8af6-7c887dd0b5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471787} {:answer/id #uuid "e70719a5-d0a8-582a-b33a-5f6433cb18b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbb5f7e3-e049-5251-8af6-7c887dd0b5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471787} :answer-field/id #uuid "41e5c317-c542-5bef-8561-f4b9b8a23fbc" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}3{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4956b231-c3b6-599c-b16a-8affdf879701" :question/math-academy-id "q-88690" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=2{x}^{4}$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =2(-x)^{4} \\\\  & =2{x}^{4} \\\\  & \\ne -f(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6(-x)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x) \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $f(x)=3{e}^{-x}$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =3{e}^{-(-x)} \\\\  & =3{e}^{x} \\\\  & \\ne -f(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049895 :topic/id #uuid "1c611a71-aaa1-5a41-a6cd-aa83bbba97af" :topic/math-academy-id 3645 :topic/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48d21b03-b4aa-5edf-97d9-e8d82ba76aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454250} {:answer/id #uuid "a4df005b-76b4-5349-9381-8a02c4118a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48d21b03-b4aa-5edf-97d9-e8d82ba76aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454250} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e0c8fb9-1191-5fbe-89aa-082fed4cfe5c" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(T)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454875} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46db31c3-b479-5b1f-9f99-dea7a4e5f9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454252} {:answer/id #uuid "6adfd406-7a7b-520c-b675-6259bd0b2894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46db31c3-b479-5b1f-9f99-dea7a4e5f9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454252} :answer-field/id #uuid "61692f77-337b-53e8-9104-052d1bee29b9" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454876} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bf8b14e-2ea8-5937-a61f-4fbf1ad7451e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454254} {:answer/id #uuid "3f5d6c2c-7493-5064-bdb2-fd8b5146ef90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f5d6c2c-7493-5064-bdb2-fd8b5146ef90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454255} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cfa9f97-b5ce-506a-a8e7-d728d9426d04" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(T)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5aa9ee11-e88d-5123-8f62-331a18227a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-97075" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ to the origin. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is the zero-subspace ${0},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=0\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$ is false. We have that\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$ is false. The condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(T)=0$ is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(T)=0$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049895 :topic/id #uuid "1c611a71-aaa1-5a41-a6cd-aa83bbba97af" :topic/math-academy-id 3645 :topic/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane"} :activity/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563964} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564586}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049895 :topic/id #uuid "1c611a71-aaa1-5a41-a6cd-aa83bbba97af" :topic/math-academy-id 3645 :topic/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "666fa542-cf57-5c1b-8235-fd0e152853d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454256} {:answer/id #uuid "011063c3-9666-5b11-8325-d5a53f0ca7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "011063c3-9666-5b11-8325-d5a53f0ca7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454257} :answer-field/id #uuid "251c5103-04e9-5f82-9799-dce064a89e0b" :answer-field/key "$⟨-1,2⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859bf573-b364-5fe7-906a-1889b6b49ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454258} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7f0115-a5c9-53d6-a054-0f8b8da7d2d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "859bf573-b364-5fe7-906a-1889b6b49ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454258} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fba21ba-604e-5a02-b4e4-86f7b393c68e" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "737fb959-5d8a-5e06-a11d-18a5e40324a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454260} {:answer/id #uuid "afff2fb7-4c9e-5490-b6a1-72764933cd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "737fb959-5d8a-5e06-a11d-18a5e40324a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454260} :answer-field/id #uuid "d766cf66-eb67-509f-bfcf-670ca1d9a88f" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(T)=0$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f9ccb581-9372-57d1-992f-f285342045f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-97080" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=-2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is a one-dimensional line, then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=1,\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $⟨-1,2⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T)$ is true. Indeed, the point $(-1,2)$ satisfies the equation of the line $y=-2x$ since $2=-2\\cdot (-1).$ Hence, \n\n$$\n⟨-1,2⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T).\n$$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}$ is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(T)=1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(T)=0$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$” is false. We have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $⟨-1,2⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "382a6db7-2708-5711-885e-6f3f3037e8df" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Functions is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048572 :topic/id #uuid "aabe8b8c-a429-5abb-824a-40f9fdf376e0" :topic/math-academy-id 2104 :topic/title "Orthogonal Sets in Inner Product Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "320d9242-a62e-5c01-9167-d38710e9024c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471809} {:answer/id #uuid "362b3fdd-9f80-5650-bbde-24dd702199b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "362b3fdd-9f80-5650-bbde-24dd702199b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471810} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd6540a6-001f-53ab-803a-662d03037eca" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472410} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8138994-dcf1-5ca7-b1d2-22437449679c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471811} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4bef01-6686-5bbb-b4b9-e6d742a886ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8138994-dcf1-5ca7-b1d2-22437449679c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471811} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ac12782-25b8-5598-a320-1aba893cb274" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472411} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15dc53de-e750-5228-914a-e0782ec8491a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471813} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d30f76-9cdf-5b19-82fb-3fe455865e34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15dc53de-e750-5228-914a-e0782ec8491a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471813} :answer-field/id #uuid "09f2dcce-48f9-5c4f-8b06-c72964cad539" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0457d3f-7a7d-578e-b127-39bac9e28900" :question/math-academy-id "q-99863" :question/problem "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=t,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,{f}_{3}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[-\\pi /2,\\pi /2]$ of continuous functions over $[-\\pi /2,\\pi /2]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is called orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩=⟨t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the integration by parts formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2}){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )}{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )}{2})+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}{4}{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =0+(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )}{4}) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{3}(t)⟩=⟨t,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the integration by parts formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}+{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =0+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =2\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{3}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "382a6db7-2708-5711-885e-6f3f3037e8df" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Functions is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048572 :topic/id #uuid "aabe8b8c-a429-5abb-824a-40f9fdf376e0" :topic/math-academy-id 2104 :topic/title "Orthogonal Sets in Inner Product Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb3f792-8daa-5481-90a3-72c22e1e0cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471815} {:answer/id #uuid "37bf6595-efed-5e05-9eea-c39ccace55ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bb3f792-8daa-5481-90a3-72c22e1e0cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471815} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef3c0786-1837-57ae-b61a-5fcc2a1ae0da" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472413} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82d9a59f-6071-55e9-ba83-81a93266ba78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471817} {:answer/id #uuid "7f4ccf74-dfd0-5457-ae1d-2f4b1376f55f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f4ccf74-dfd0-5457-ae1d-2f4b1376f55f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471818} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4772d99-ef37-508b-be2b-5bf2236274df" :answer-field/key "${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472414} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "983ffe32-ea8e-5549-a804-3f8a808db229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471819} {:answer/id #uuid "9b9010c5-b935-59a9-aa88-3c4656c8a125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "983ffe32-ea8e-5549-a804-3f8a808db229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471819} :answer-field/id #uuid "9241636c-59e4-57aa-90d4-9f47ca3f6f1e" :answer-field/key "$S={{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "866dfd7d-0156-5915-b7a2-48bb304694df" :question/math-academy-id "q-99949" :question/problem "Consider the following set of functions:\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,{f}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{f}_{3}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[-\\pi /2,\\pi /2]$ of continuous functions over $[-\\pi /2,\\pi /2]$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨f(t),g(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is called orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)⟩=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the identity $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)⟩=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ differentiating we have $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$ Hence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{sin}^{2}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that ${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S={{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t),{f}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${f}_{1}(t)⊥̸{f}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{2}(t)⊥{f}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048572 :topic/id #uuid "aabe8b8c-a429-5abb-824a-40f9fdf376e0" :topic/math-academy-id 2104 :topic/title "Orthogonal Sets in Inner Product Spaces"} :activity/title "Orthogonal Sets in Inner Product Spaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517479} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518288}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c915f3d8-89f2-53ed-aef0-20b410b54630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453150} {:answer/id #uuid "3f37584d-1373-5be8-ac5a-8410240fe69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f37584d-1373-5be8-ac5a-8410240fe69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453151} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6c663f3-33fc-5e6d-b766-632d1b4cd482" :answer-field/key "$f(-1)\\ne f(1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbf1e044-84c3-5f30-a402-f435bec02e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453152} {:answer/id #uuid "b6dee32f-9add-502d-baa1-906900439c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6dee32f-9add-502d-baa1-906900439c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453153} :answer-field/id #uuid "99235344-66bd-542f-8c3c-ebc972c3c1c0" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454326} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a477356-2383-5fed-af7d-7bac2355443f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453154} {:answer/id #uuid "6878e6e9-6904-523a-bf6f-59f21f65cbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6878e6e9-6904-523a-bf6f-59f21f65cbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453155} :answer-field/id #uuid "00328259-8f3e-5a30-b032-16741e404afb" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b421e9a7-e6c7-514b-9eac-4c4a22d0b15a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105133" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=x+2?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/3b/3b849edf2ae8976e0abd5e0aa43180ad61d90b01d6f229c2b7fc7898ea860400.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-1)\\ne f(1)$ is true. We have $f(-1)=(-1)+2=1$ and $f(1)=1+2=3.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $R$ that map to the same element in $R.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(-1)\\ne f(1)$; “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$”; “$f$ is an injection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa306f54-ba80-566c-a82a-6904584a1e66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470769} {:answer/id #uuid "a729fd60-80e0-5f99-8453-328c9947e595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa306f54-ba80-566c-a82a-6904584a1e66" :answer/type 