r-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "212414c0-44d6-50de-aa8e-6b4bd0efa627" :question/math-academy-id "q-105202" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8f4d72bd431d4f06daa3ea2be20d0ebb21fd736b944be77331c72c2e47e3144f.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[0,\\infty ]\\to (-\\infty ,5]$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(0)=f(2)$ is false. According to the graph, we have $f(0)=5$ and $f(2)<5.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [0,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[0,\\infty )$ that map to the same element in $(-\\infty ,5].$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[0,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **one-to-one**” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [0,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true, $f$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [0,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$”; “$f$ is **one-to-one**” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee9c51fe-1f93-5f07-8dfb-54553964dbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470775} {:answer/id #uuid "be8844ed-55c4-59b2-b7f6-dbf5de4e307e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9c51fe-1f93-5f07-8dfb-54553964dbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470775} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6115a53-5892-5b95-b119-f5eb572d5212" :answer-field/key "$f(-2)\\ne f(2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8a1014a-6170-583a-a39e-d8ba72176fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470777} {:answer/id #uuid "176a2196-a6d5-5fb9-84b6-11cad8e38f0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8a1014a-6170-583a-a39e-d8ba72176fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470777} :answer-field/id #uuid "2641bae7-0817-5b22-9386-7370addc7324" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de4b935-368e-5457-a4f8-db8dfd1a7594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470779} {:answer/id #uuid "b7dab165-506c-51cc-b247-9891d757f656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7dab165-506c-51cc-b247-9891d757f656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470780} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e8260e3-2830-52f4-92c1-0a618d01500a" :answer-field/key "$f$ is not an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41a4e16b-532b-5af9-a855-bdbc2ac881f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-105203" :question/problem "![](images/64/64b81ef8b99a70ae69b607b9c9440e9588576f8ea2243a8aa82f52d92bde8630.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,2]\\to [-1,5]$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-2)\\ne f(2)$ is false. According to the graph, we have $f(-2)=f(2)=5.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false. Again, we have $f(-2)=f(2)$ but $-2\\ne 2.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is not an injection” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false, $f$ is not an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is not an injection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf5d37a-6a00-5f10-8c55-9bbf970be92f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453156} {:answer/id #uuid "7aabeaaa-3849-5d13-a1f9-585d16f30b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aabeaaa-3849-5d13-a1f9-585d16f30b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453157} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d09a131-c0e0-5472-9310-cb6dc878fd2b" :answer-field/key "$f(-1)=f(1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454328} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6a85fcb-471d-59b8-8bbf-b61ac06e8c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453158} {:answer/id #uuid "42f1bfb9-3ee8-576b-8d94-62e4e82fe7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6a85fcb-471d-59b8-8bbf-b61ac06e8c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453158} :answer-field/id #uuid "858a3d04-ac8a-53d5-a5f5-9dc8ece2494a" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4785ad13-bddb-53ce-98ae-ef532d0b5549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453160} {:answer/id #uuid "43d8aafb-36cd-57c5-ae2b-29091b7a792b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d8aafb-36cd-57c5-ae2b-29091b7a792b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453161} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c4e34de-81f1-556d-93cf-cdcb98a4c2df" :answer-field/key "$f$ is not **one-to-one**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0c99dc3-deba-5ffb-83d8-510a75eea6dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-105206" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,2]\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{3}-x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/86/869be2ef6cb317b81c249b85b0afcbea23178dcf3bb77bb008e69375494439df.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-1)=f(1)$ is true. We have $f(-1)=\\frac{1}{2}((-1)^{3}-(-1))=0$ and $f(1)=\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{3}-1)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false. We have $f(-1)=f(1)$ but $-1\\ne 1.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is not **one-to-one**” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(-1)=f(1)$; “$f$ is not **one-to-one**” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382764 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f60da9a5-46b9-5640-917a-84d152500b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470781} {:answer/id #uuid "db67b4ba-51c5-5307-b54f-071736122164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db67b4ba-51c5-5307-b54f-071736122164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470782} :answer-field/id #uuid "23a37e11-3e5a-5d77-ac6f-dd421e0cec52" :answer-field/key "$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad6ab3d1-3a72-54da-9273-f6968bc86b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470783} {:answer/id #uuid "25b3c95f-a837-516d-b120-06235ea8ed7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25b3c95f-a837-516d-b120-06235ea8ed7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470784} :answer-field/id #uuid "92fb8256-feb1-5dc4-b383-cab83629ca77" :answer-field/key "$g:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471897} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfb43541-28e2-5f49-995a-083e58df47fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470785} {:answer/id #uuid "25f24fc0-8a87-523a-b40c-0775b54838dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfb43541-28e2-5f49-995a-083e58df47fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470785} :answer-field/id #uuid "6060b62c-dc47-56b2-a681-49a4bebd2456" :answer-field/key "$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=(x+1)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a4c4299-1d16-58a6-b63b-ffcefd188616" :question/math-academy-id "q-105218" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$” is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {2}^{{x}_{1}} & ={2}^{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡{2}^{{x}_{1}} & ={log}_{2}⁡{2}^{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- “$g:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$” is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{1}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{2}} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- “$h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=(x+1)^{2}$” is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(-2),$ but $0\\ne -2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$”; “$g:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eace52b-7e6e-5ec8-b519-3c4941f46c31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470787} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb5d57f-63a6-5a6d-8168-fb5fce1121eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bb5d57f-63a6-5a6d-8168-fb5fce1121eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470788} :answer-field/id #uuid "b953bfa5-4a49-5115-8695-97ca60313935" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b678175d-5703-57e2-a818-f6453b55fa13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470789} {:answer/id #uuid "d274bcce-f637-54a1-a37c-89d6ebd6489b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d274bcce-f637-54a1-a37c-89d6ebd6489b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470790} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1779ddf-7824-52f2-a5da-31f0049c6613" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471900} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfbc10a7-9ed9-50ea-a8d4-7fb24bb1cdb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470791} {:answer/id #uuid "515b6786-c3f0-596c-984e-79d5fc618129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "515b6786-c3f0-596c-984e-79d5fc618129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470792} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c02af87-593e-51e0-bb13-98a4fee0c423" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db660bb9-e18a-5aa6-8b12-2d9637cff073" :question/math-academy-id "q-105224" :question/problem "![](images/32/32957c5f0b4eeb76253f9fe812e2025b93a2cd5c65870f5a0b3608ce545dd4c5.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is true. Indeed, according to the diagram, for every element $y\\in Y,$ we have an arrow from some element $x\\in X$ to it, which means that $f(x)=y.$ So, $f$ is a surjection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a bijection” is true. Indeed, since both statements “$f$ is a surjection” and “$f$ is an injection” are true, $f$ is a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is a surjection”; “$f$ is an injection”; “$f$ is a bijection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc7992a8-cbb3-5f8e-b007-ab2ea5c813c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470793} {:answer/id #uuid "627bad4d-8ca6-5d60-b2fd-b12f774dd599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc7992a8-cbb3-5f8e-b007-ab2ea5c813c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470793} :answer-field/id #uuid "d09a6756-7c54-5df1-83bf-1c051b12f7aa" :answer-field/key "$f:{R}^{+}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17067fdc-9575-5d08-b671-4d5101e4f4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470795} {:answer/id #uuid "4993eed4-7e10-5d8c-a0fa-3496eb439b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4993eed4-7e10-5d8c-a0fa-3496eb439b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470796} :answer-field/id #uuid "1573b02e-10cf-571c-b610-1d0af069a79b" :answer-field/key "$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2a2f550-1205-5ab3-8c67-1cff3710b415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470797} {:answer/id #uuid "0f3071a0-962f-59c5-89d2-11d4116dfefb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2a2f550-1205-5ab3-8c67-1cff3710b415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470797} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9c4350-7308-57a6-a282-f2e31192a4ca" :answer-field/key "$h:Q\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)=|x|$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aad509f8-bb58-5f68-8c6d-48ccc6e72f00" :question/math-academy-id "q-105283" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- “$f:{R}^{+}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$” is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Remember that the range of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is $f(x)\\in (0,\\infty )$ for $x\\in {R}^{+}.$ So, for example, there is no value $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-1.$\n\n- “$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{3}$” is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in R,$ we can choose an $x\\in R$ such that $g(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =y \\\\ {x}^{3} & =y \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{y}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that\n\n$$\ng(x)=g(\\sqrt[3]{y})={(\\sqrt[3]{y})}^{3}=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}^{3} & ={x}_{2}^{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause $g$ is both surjective and injective, $g$ is bijective.\n\n- “$h:Q\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)=|x|$” is *not* a bijection because it is not injective. Notice that $h(-1)=1=h(1),$ while $-1\\ne 1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{3}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2c9854-e7ac-53f2-a35a-667b5e538e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470799} {:answer/id #uuid "273245b8-208f-51e1-814d-16128312ef4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "273245b8-208f-51e1-814d-16128312ef4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470800} :answer-field/id #uuid "8679fb50-7f40-5989-91bf-6a37ac64cb52" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0390169-c968-53ca-8fb1-cc3655a138a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470801} {:answer/id #uuid "42bfce10-71b7-53e0-b55e-8f5dd5952cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0390169-c968-53ca-8fb1-cc3655a138a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470801} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f809694-9ddd-57d6-9777-83898e22464a" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df722798-512e-55d5-a9b7-354ded28b7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470803} {:answer/id #uuid "2196f15f-b9da-537e-a5c0-f5fda218a028" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df722798-512e-55d5-a9b7-354ded28b7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470803} :answer-field/id #uuid "aff16c98-c4a1-5aa2-8323-5bdd382b01a9" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab6d4262-72da-5293-84a5-c795900dbdb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-105302" :question/problem "![](images/70/707aad3ee7b52647cdc565aee76a4276aee01c8369236f24908f1c89d234e588.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R∖{-1}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=1-\\frac{1}{x+1}$, which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/86/8605d88b3187d6e8444e5cb7a8c591ab4e67b781cfba79c119fa11e5696c13a1.png)\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. There is no value $x$ for which $f(x)=1.$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The function is an injection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eefa4b28-cfbc-5fed-8f61-128fe905dd59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470805} {:answer/id #uuid "a5adc7a1-f0b1-57d6-b194-14cd857d88db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eefa4b28-cfbc-5fed-8f61-128fe905dd59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470805} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac60148-9d3a-50f6-95bd-ac00310202e2" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f2c96c7-edd4-5c51-964e-2e801fc8aa42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470807} {:answer/id #uuid "86a56401-de1b-53ab-af0c-cd348987fbc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86a56401-de1b-53ab-af0c-cd348987fbc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470808} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6bc75ec-b0bd-57d6-a49d-6bf697b0c484" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471909} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49b6ea0f-6e25-5a4e-89a1-f9549433134d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470809} {:answer/id #uuid "12572af4-5601-51b1-8ae5-d8a93d7ddb5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49b6ea0f-6e25-5a4e-89a1-f9549433134d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470809} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbdecc36-32a4-563e-90e8-b7581ff9500f" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8df77440-bcac-5064-a5e6-fdeeaf2cd8d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-105305" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5f7c319a0648cdefc0c6a7ba40e6df62a88df92c8bc87fdaadf2afdca46ae0d6.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R,$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. There are horizontal lines (like the one depicted below) that cross the graph of $f(x)$ more than once. So, $∃\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that ${x}_{1}\\ne {x}_{2}$ but $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}).$\n\n![](images/bd/bdd421bdd147eb8d0dc9fc593a1205b9a4665bc6d3a3cb76ec7f2e3bf518ecb6.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is true. According to the graph, the range of $f(x)$ will cover the entire interval $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false. Indeed, since statement “The function is an injection” is false, $f$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The function is a surjection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382799 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dec32e79-8bd4-5baa-be98-3d73c4b7b061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470811} {:answer/id #uuid "2e88dd84-a796-5643-942c-161aac781ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e88dd84-a796-5643-942c-161aac781ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470812} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f26d264-51ff-5e57-9325-a85ddc45d56e" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65b8f445-8ede-5e38-845d-a0b97d9a5b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470813} {:answer/id #uuid "40bdb041-cb1b-5289-b601-e1d3241bc4cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65b8f445-8ede-5e38-845d-a0b97d9a5b02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470813} :answer-field/id #uuid "202ada3e-ef2c-5129-b965-c43d832f8e22" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ec51a8c-4a3b-5554-b87b-e75f58b5c63e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470815} {:answer/id #uuid "012f9f56-9c3e-5409-8f3d-6095a5ee028c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ec51a8c-4a3b-5554-b87b-e75f58b5c63e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470815} :answer-field/id #uuid "5945f5a2-7696-5d2b-823d-98afa1042edc" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09bf6284-af1f-5fbe-9b83-9ea47f00c38a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105307" :question/problem "![](images/84/84755249e491fd44868098e8edccfd32cffda23a5859f0a9df293b57b4353040.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to [0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{-x}$, which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/01/016b83dcbb2f2008d428fb52ba26336b35fa0af0d67e435d06122845f3492b2e.png)\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. Indeed, ${2}^{-x}>0$ for all $x\\in R.$ So, there is no value $x$ such that $f(x)=0\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\n Therefore, the correct answer is “The function is an injection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382806 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14b541a7-5e26-504a-b052-7e92cc233d4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answ