nswer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470822} :answer-field/id #uuid "61e53737-4eb4-54cd-be32-14482ec6f23b" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09033cd1-e3bd-58ad-8df5-2396d7439d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-105329" :question/problem "![](images/5c/5c50beff59a4bc2ae8cf3da8c9fed849c73cbf828ad0f875675520fc33589365.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x-1}$, which of the following statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is true. Any horizontal line (like the one depicted below) crosses the graph of $f(x)$ at most once.\n\n![](images/66/66d558a2118721b2793311fb0f4687d91aefa125e74a73379c793a9fdbedf46d.png)\n\n        \n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is true. According to the graph, the range of $f(x)$ will cover the entire interval $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is true because the function is both surjective and injective.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The function is an injection”; “The function is a surjection”; “The function is a bijection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fbd78fe-5ede-5795-9622-962461ceaffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470823} {:answer/id #uuid "9de6e2bf-f8e9-549b-9aed-e689c26328e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fbd78fe-5ede-5795-9622-962461ceaffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470823} :answer-field/id #uuid "3837b8ab-5872-5992-97f4-40787670506a" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca534b3e-7b8d-50f0-8361-4fe1356e93d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470825} {:answer/id #uuid "d603d976-e8c8-5eb2-8c88-cea3ab366fdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca534b3e-7b8d-50f0-8361-4fe1356e93d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470825} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4e0316e-a490-5722-a171-17b4936ef2c1" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471918} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c5d5dc3-30a6-556f-a142-ba2a5ab13561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470827} {:answer/id #uuid "551313b9-9c31-565f-bd3f-853edba26752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c5d5dc3-30a6-556f-a142-ba2a5ab13561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470827} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f1b659c-be5a-5301-b7ea-21955cb2e5fa" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea34001e-7666-5760-9335-3a797f196771" :question/math-academy-id "q-105330" :question/problem "![](images/88/8845d8cc2664c92637e06961f1d5c17b98afcb72470d1463fbd58aaf5691ca4c.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=(x+1)^{2}-2$, which of the following statements are true?  \n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. There are horizontal lines (such as the one depicted below) that cross the graph of $f(x)$ more than once.\n\n![](images/d6/d6b2a99811341aa07bc3e91df973504fad57ac4a71a38406707b5d311247d61d.png)\n\n        \n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. For example, there is not $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-4.$ So, $f$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false, because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049459 :topic/id #uuid "f6fd4776-56f0-5112-9cdc-83e344004d93" :topic/math-academy-id 2131 :topic/title "The Divergence of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67a23b89-2744-50f5-80ee-0e41d4401774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437438} {:answer/id #uuid "1e5e0906-c5a6-5260-a5c9-800e874c6cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e5e0906-c5a6-5260-a5c9-800e874c6cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437439} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ef5597b-7d44-55ff-944c-918cec802871" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cadfff51-416c-52a1-9b9d-aa9d8266ea73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437440} {:answer/id #uuid "118cf593-0894-584e-986e-b0ede741bec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cadfff51-416c-52a1-9b9d-aa9d8266ea73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437440} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1ff3919-7299-53ed-b07e-1da167e1b01d" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438749} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d16b1a8b-6a8d-5700-920b-072cfc4fe106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437442} {:answer/id #uuid "98622a4d-b944-5087-89c2-2495f60f347d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d16b1a8b-6a8d-5700-920b-072cfc4fe106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437442} :answer-field/id #uuid "5448d02c-650e-516b-a781-6d0ace7f3f1f" :answer-field/key "$\\text{div}\\,F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438750} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d2f285-2227-527f-b977-6ae8cb61cf69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437444} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d1b2e7-aa8a-576b-a9e4-c806af278c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0d1b2e7-aa8a-576b-a9e4-c806af278c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437445} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a53885c-bf18-56a8-a814-76839979dcab" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2ed7472-9bdb-5c0c-a495-7db6294676ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-105577" :question/problem "![](images/13/13b252e1f9a66836cbd72fbea9bb4c143a71344c923e2215a7718d75c9c42e26.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{div}\\,F=0$ is true, whereas statements $\\text{div}\\,F>0$ and $\\text{div}\\,F<0$ are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{div}\\,F=0$; “$F$ is solenoidal” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051085 :topic/id #uuid "7fdf89be-7454-5a23-9d34-17c62e869eea" :topic/math-academy-id 2132 :topic/title "The Curl of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d228b638-d4d7-5016-bf8d-0f56d5c4fadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437454} {:answer/id #uuid "95914e2c-927b-55a2-922e-4d9800a2f38d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d228b638-d4d7-5016-bf8d-0f56d5c4fadc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437454} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b934add-e755-50b4-b067-100e72fc3b58" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bd1d98c-7ae9-55ca-9482-d88b90b0af24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437456} {:answer/id #uuid "e43b1943-3654-567b-9fed-68e4254f3b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e43b1943-3654-567b-9fed-68e4254f3b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437457} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6ddf4cd-c05f-5097-8310-bbb48f377de3" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e686502-6511-5a87-9141-3f040b14bb72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437458} {:answer/id #uuid "d0bb29aa-53cb-587d-8e87-04375c2d7a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0bb29aa-53cb-587d-8e87-04375c2d7a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437459} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8779a01-b29f-51f0-ab0b-183634a90544" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0077624-dbc3-55a6-9c6d-142323470d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437460} {:answer/id #uuid "3165d50d-3b7d-5943-9785-4266dd0bd54a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0077624-dbc3-55a6-9c6d-142323470d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437460} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bdf6bee-a19c-5f09-acb1-0c8cf50d5033" :answer-field/key "$F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b44da0aa-9add-572b-86e2-310e134b6864" :question/math-academy-id "q-105664" :question/problem "![](images/56/5643e87bfb5dfb5c29750f48abffe2443bf656901d74a47a0aa39bddfd0c1590.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has a curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/86/86aee33cdfa96ac0a61468cc9657e791e399f31c024cdbc3a932193dc897d534.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate clockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\n- Statement “$F$ is irrotational” is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$; “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051085 :topic/id #uuid "7fdf89be-7454-5a23-9d34-17c62e869eea" :topic/math-academy-id 2132 :topic/title "The Curl of a Vector Field"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbe322f2-3c81-5a3f-8384-a79b47c4192c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437494} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9d57fd-6acd-56c1-9f2e-b83a1aa501a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd9d57fd-6acd-56c1-9f2e-b83a1aa501a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437495} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898a42c-a0be-50b6-8124-860e6bfc10bd" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438776} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ebb3d1f-b473-5ff0-99dc-159e666e7930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437496} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f04e94-0931-5901-b36f-4cf0aefffcb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ebb3d1f-b473-5ff0-99dc-159e666e7930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437496} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f5874c9-61e8-5f41-9f79-2b146b618ffd" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438777} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d37dd19-280c-5e67-ae16-cb2d1a8d8768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437498} {:answer/id #uuid "82315627-af21-5603-83df-7fa71a175af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d37dd19-280c-5e67-ae16-cb2d1a8d8768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437498} :answer-field/id #uuid "87749995-78bc-517b-80a4-3ef44008acb3" :answer-field/key "$F$ is not irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6a54cb-d3b8-527e-8166-9d17d4c66cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437500} {:answer/id #uuid "f7668637-64a8-52ae-aa22-7ac35611bf2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e6a54cb-d3b8-527e-8166-9d17d4c66cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437500} :answer-field/id #uuid "b01a01c4-08c1-5b79-8565-85e0e916e53a" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "73b73866-28ec-57e7-b02e-d1bd053c3918" :question/math-academy-id "q-105693" :question/problem "![](images/10/10a9960200e87e1b7b8a38789d5f70f29e48ad1f0a6e2913713da90c532eca6e.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is true, whereas statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements “$F$ is not irrotational” and “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction” are false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational. And, since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172016 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3e3fdc8-67d0-5b46-9c6b-c1ec8d4ea24f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048885 :topic/id #uuid "c96ee93a-fd82-595c-824f-e11934066ffc" :topic/math-academy-id 3350 :topic/title "Analyzing Slope Fields for Nonautonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59c2108e-96b3-5d6e-b962-726f73a1c21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470907} {:answer/id #uuid "29a4d37b-cc9d-5abd-be6e-cfa2b43602c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29a4d37b-cc9d-5abd-be6e-cfa2b43602c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470908} :answer-field/id #uuid "abd7be65-6a56-5d33-8320-4a5183336838" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{y+2}{x-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471959} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abb4d5de-82bb-5735-b761-cfde599aa37d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470909} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed146ce-9654-5b05-8813-205e6efe5487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb4d5de-82bb-5735-b761-cfde599aa37d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470909} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c7baf85-0e15-56af-8e13-67a4b94d7bb9" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=(x-1)(y-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f62e0438-6fb4-597d-b819-130688cdb78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470911} {:answer/id #uuid "634a9e82-263e-5ffd-abd8-8a03e7ee5d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f62e0438-6fb4-597d-b819-130688cdb78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470911} :answer-field/id #uuid "0aa2ffea-ff43-5b1d-90a1-15f52b173f02" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}=\\frac{y-2}{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9198e7bb-f6e2-569d-9a58-c321fc238e98" :question/math-academy-id "q-120290" :question/problem "![](images/32/32fefe70890d179803a847fc597349948703176d1561a8c840e845fa7a06a872.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/a1/a18f69bf5b2cb6b2984722f851e1eda017e48863517da7ee65597d7c25c46379.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- For $x\\ne 1,$ the slopes of the slope field become horizontal at $y=-2.$\n\n- For $y\\ne -2,$ the slopes of the slope field become vertical as $x\\to 1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y+2}{x-1}$ gives the required behavior. For $x\\ne 1,$ the right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y+2}{x-1}$ evaluates to zero on $y=-2,$ and for $y\\ne -2,$\n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{y+2}{x-1}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 1.\n$$\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=(x-1)(y-2)$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=(x-1)(y-2)$ does not evaluate to zero on $y=-2$ (the value depends on $x$).\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y-2}{x}$ does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y-2}{x}$ evaluates to zero on $y=2,$ but \n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{y-2}{x}|\\to |y-2|\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y+2}{x-1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65adbd80-9647-59d8-bd4a-42f431587c85" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Conservative Vector Fields" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050983 :topic/id #uuid "76f021c9-2347-5c45-873f-1f9d1e3473c8" :topic/math-academy-id 3149 :topic/title "Conservative Vector Fields in the Cartesian Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e78342e-7073-5996-b8d2-29a251917883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437704} {:answer/id #uuid "1d04d934-dcdb-526f-b570-2dbcc6fce5a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d04d934-dcdb-526f-b570-2dbcc6fce5a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437705} :answer-field/id #uuid "b474b307-7652-5024-93ce-3d6d184d1386" :answer-field/key "$F=x{y}^{2}\\,i+{x}^{2}y\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65dc72a9-ac06-5f1a-bf28-b0607daf1e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437706} {:answer/id #uuid "a136b1c8-384b-51aa-80e4-6450fc364d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65dc72a9-ac06-5f1a-bf28-b0607daf1e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437706} :answer-field/id #uuid "70c7e673-aa45-56c5-83bc-18fb8c69889f" :answer-field/key "$G=2x\\,i-3(x+y)\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0467504c-f5ba-5c65-b935-abce7630a7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437708} {:answer/id #uuid "fab9a31b-ee2c-52cf-8167-c9659890b4a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0467504c-f5ba-5c65-b935-abce7630a7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437708} :answer-field/id #uuid "8654b8c1-2a6a-54eb-b934-803e7b9c7856" :answer-field/key "$H={e}^{x-y}\\,i+{e}^{y-x}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f81692c-bc38-55e0-9228-b9c2fd15506d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123866" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields.\n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=x{y}^{2}$ and $Q={x}^{2}y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=2x$ and $Q=-3(x+y).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $G$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P={e}^{x-y}$ and $Q={e}^{y-x}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{x-y},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-{e}^{y-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $H$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $F=x{y}^{2}\\,i+{x}^{2}y\\,j$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Pairs of First-Order Partial Derivatives" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049696 :topic/id #uuid "0bfad6b0-12ee-58d9-8324-1f301647b82f" :topic/math-academy-id 1957 :topic/title "Equality of Mixed Partial Derivatives"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56a20be7-6579-511c-ad5d-1ce303fce86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471009} {:answer/id #uuid "a847bdd2-d7bd-5d0a-b7be-52597a69380f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a847bdd2-d7bd-5d0a-b7be-52597a69380f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471010} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb111a44-39df-585c-967b-ae6f35ecc6d6" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=6{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=6xy$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bc76465-5b80-50ab-bc52-afc8e762680f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471011} {:answer/id #uuid "5782df2a-d54b-5db6-b27f-35c713430005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bc76465-5b80-50ab-bc52-afc8e762680f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471011} :answer-field/id #uuid "b963fb55-cead-5821-b0dc-816138d8b25a" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=15{x}^{2}-y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=8y+x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5cc124a-3892-5225-a9c7-6e32907d06fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471013} {:answer/id #uuid "5b51995a-55f7-5346-b0ce-8a490c88d9e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b51995a-55f7-5346-b0ce-8a490c88d9e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471014} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2d30c3d-5554-5a5b-a121-14874855257e" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-3{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472012}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "017164c5-337a-58b5-8e66-674d944a6841" :question/math-academy-id "q-133262" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2})=6y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6xy)=6y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(15{x}^{2}-y)=-1 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8y+x)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2})=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$,  the third pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{x}(x,y)=6{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=6xy$”; “${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-3{y}^{2}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Pairs of First-Order Partial Derivatives" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049696 :topic/id #uuid "0bfad6b0-12ee-58d9-8324-1f301647b82f" :topic/math-academy-id 1957 :topic/title "Equality of Mixed Partial Derivatives"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ba2ae8e-668d-5174-a86d-2cf8dc8cac78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471015} {:answer/id #uuid "0f322749-ca06-58f8-9b9e-c84f76987f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ba2ae8e-668d-5174-a86d-2cf8dc8cac78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471015} :answer-field/id #uuid "414a4e94-a112-586d-b5d5-a8053d338a4b" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x})$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472013} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b088d5b8-a6f1-5b21-9fd5-d1d92b01b633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471017} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b69fff-cb92-543e-a99b-18e346dc344c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6b69fff-cb92-543e-a99b-18e346dc344c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471018} :answer-field/id #uuid "175f313c-b8a0-5f41-a622-5331199d6a62" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\sqrt{1-y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472014} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "825ef8ce-26f3-5554-add9-7a2866d49ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471019} {:answer/id #uuid "87b03dd6-e89c-544c-9a74-9b059df6f464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "825ef8ce-26f3-5554-add9-7a2866d49ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471019} :answer-field/id #uuid "20c03c3b-8284-571c-ba36-765ccd7b8f09" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "004baeb6-1fe8-58d6-b484-d81ddf229838" :question/math-academy-id "q-133295" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x}))=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{x}))={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}})=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{1-y})=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1))=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1))=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\sqrt{1-y}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Pairs of First-Order Partial Derivatives" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049696 :topic/id #uuid "0bfad6b0-12ee-58d9-8324-1f301647b82f" :topic/math-academy-id 1957 :topic/title "Equality of Mixed Partial Derivatives"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b02ff6f-57e0-536c-aca3-2d760268e2c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471021} {:answer/id #uuid "c872f2f6-b7d6-5c29-bbde-7c4b15738fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c872f2f6-b7d6-5c29-bbde-7c4b15738fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471022} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f381ca-9503-5ca4-b72b-7b29cf5f410e" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=2{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2y{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d88b8d-cf78-5d26-9ffa-9f547e94dd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471023} {:answer/id #uuid "95c494e0-4cde-5941-b742-7701608869a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06d88b8d-cf78-5d26-9ffa-9f547e94dd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471023} :answer-field/id #uuid "676c65d2-db56-5535-9e55-00232223631f" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e39de23b-aee0-5777-af07-2bf8ce165ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471025} {:answer/id #uuid "8122d886-265c-54ae-9df9-1489be890b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e39de23b-aee0-5777-af07-2bf8ce165ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471025} :answer-field/id #uuid "1578bce8-93a1-52a1-8300-d409929c6425" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d4e7c93-f352-516f-9253-b49a36a438e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-133297" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}})=-4y{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y{e}^{2x+{y}^{2}})=-4y{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2}))=4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{y}^{2}) \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2}))=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})+4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{x})=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the third pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{x}(x,y)=2{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2y{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Pairs of First-Order Partial Derivatives" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049696 :topic/id #uuid "0bfad6b0-12ee-58d9-8324-1f301647b82f" :topic/math-academy-id 1957 :topic/title "Equality of Mixed Partial Derivatives"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be14b852-a6af-555c-bbdf-afdaf5cc630a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471027} {:answer/id #uuid "76e6636e-da82-541f-a918-44d3e2909381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be14b852-a6af-555c-bbdf-afdaf5cc630a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471027} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4e454b2-9b73-579b-88fd-8f6234445d79" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)={x}^{2}+5y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=3{x}^{2}-3y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a1843c6-0d23-5144-9c62-7cc65106b7fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471029} {:answer/id #uuid "308507af-652e-5dd7-ba73-937e3e345d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308507af-652e-5dd7-ba73-937e3e345d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471030} :answer-field/id #uuid "9359ed1e-6c6c-5066-83f7-d8cc6ede1470" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=-2x{e}^{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a715f9-ee83-5ec5-aeab-43274076ad6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471031} {:answer/id #uuid "464eba41-9a20-5cac-8bd1-fef80526f565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "464eba41-9a20-5cac-8bd1-fef80526f565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471032} :answer-field/id #uuid "851cbb8b-c023-503e-8cb0-c20dd5104f10" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y-y{e}^{xy}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={x}^{3}-x{e}^{xy}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffcfd211-dc96-5e56-a933-77ab3f803324" :question/math-academy-id "q-133332" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+5y)=5 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-3y)=6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2x{e}^{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}})=-6x{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}})=-6x{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}y-y{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-({e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}), \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-x{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-({e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the third pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{x}(x,y)=-2x{e}^{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}}$”; “${f}_{x}(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y-y{e}^{xy}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={x}^{3}-x{e}^{xy}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050835 :topic/id #uuid "6a5936fb-0bab-5b84-a342-e13ec8019ebc" :topic/math-academy-id 3048 :topic/title "Independence of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b7c73a6-2af0-5b92-b6f9-3d93e71ac279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453410} {:answer/id #uuid "cd588ae9-2b60-5171-90a5-e75b1b1f4e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd588ae9-2b60-5171-90a5-e75b1b1f4e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453411} :answer-field/id #uuid "e212ea0e-0893-522d-b146-c4a56808a680" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=2)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454455} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e69a34-93a1-5a43-834c-4e189751c4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453412} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4c23a1-a357-5eb9-9f99-65ce1db5f659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d4c23a1-a357-5eb9-9f99-65ce1db5f659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453413} :answer-field/id #uuid "79de55e8-6943-548b-a367-c214c3149889" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454456} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f17d2094-f158-54e5-846d-74fedf6ed19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453414} {:answer/id #uuid "68e664fb-4f6e-51e7-b3d4-8922d50069a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68e664fb-4f6e-51e7-b3d4-8922d50069a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453415} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed06e01-142b-5c2b-b22f-d3c32e2dbb48" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47bb5e3d-7de9-53ad-b629-7512a9b347ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-143328" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ | $0.75$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=1,Y=2)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=2)=f(1,2)=0.15.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.25\\cdot 0.6=0.15.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =0.1=0.25\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(2,1) & =0.3=0.75\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(2,2) & =0.45=0.75\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is true. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=1,Y=2)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)$; “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$”; “$X$ and $Y$ are independent”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050835 :topic/id #uuid "6a5936fb-0bab-5b84-a342-e13ec8019ebc" :topic/math-academy-id 3048 :topic/title "Independence of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98db4bdf-35c0-572f-a8d0-dd5af5d2d797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471045} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5b1cde-3a17-5c26-ae0b-684c07d6c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e5b1cde-3a17-5c26-ae0b-684c07d6c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471046} :answer-field/id #uuid "28b9829d-7120-5b5c-92bd-c1ef0c0e2fa6" :answer-field/key "$P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472028} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9127507d-cd00-5560-bb89-a83a30f508fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471047} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4074bd-8e93-5f12-a606-f60e237bc602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9127507d-cd00-5560-bb89-a83a30f508fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471047} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbaf59b-eeb3-51ce-8a01-5dc52517e99d" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472029} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf59bd71-a0bd-5b9f-a650-5a3684e0a341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471049} {:answer/id #uuid "ee3117e1-426e-540f-a519-e302a751ae0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf59bd71-a0bd-5b9f-a650-5a3684e0a341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471049} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d335f5-b08f-5856-be51-b11cb49c2f5f" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5449cbef-825d-5bac-be24-822940400b4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-143335" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=2,Y=2)=f(2,2)=0.2.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.5\\cdot 0.4=0.2.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Taking $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =0.1\\ne 0.2\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198400 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4179839d-85c4-5325-9293-e332bd209597" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Inverse Function Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048251 :topic/id #uuid "8c7bb5de-2e24-552b-9fb3-2501f210a725" :topic/math-academy-id 4149 :topic/title "The Inverse Function Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dfbfd1f-8c57-5fbe-a046-ceb729aa8a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471131} {:answer/id #uuid "73106404-c5ab-5410-828f-e3512801d032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dfbfd1f-8c57-5fbe-a046-ceb729aa8a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471131} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff7b3c6d-8c28-54e5-9c3d-44c52e635b0b" :answer-field/key "The function $f$ is invertible on $U.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8d21e81-e466-5275-b6d7-e8596ffd6af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471133} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea8393e-8b7e-5757-8a39-9abbd88090d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8d21e81-e466-5275-b6d7-e8596ffd6af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471133} :answer-field/id #uuid "8576233d-a2de-53f9-8fb3-a010c3910212" :answer-field/key "The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable on $U.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c413dcb0-496c-5788-83c8-a5743c676e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471135} {:answer/id #uuid "490e1529-0fed-5e20-985c-3761de5fd52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490e1529-0fed-5e20-985c-3761de5fd52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471136} :answer-field/id #uuid "885433fd-1178-5da3-bd21-57f732fa2bb4" :answer-field/key "The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4dcab08e-c33d-5c73-a45a-265b0e425858" :question/math-academy-id "q-161847" :question/problem "Let $f:U\\to R$ be continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R$ such that $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U.$ Which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The function $f$ is invertible on $U.$” is false. According to the theorem, the function $f$ must be invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$ which could be smaller than $U.$ \n\nFor example, the function $f(x)=2{x}^{4}$ satisfies the conditions of the inverse function theorem for $U=(-2,2)$ and $a=-1.$ However, $f(x)$ is not invertible on the entire set $U,$ only on a subset of $U.$\n\n- Statement “The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable on $U.$” is false. According to the theorem, the function${f}^{-1}$ must be continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ which could be smaller than $U.$\n\n- Statement “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$” is true. According to the theorem, we must have ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198400 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4179839d-85c4-5325-9293-e332bd209597" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Inverse Function Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048251 :topic/id #uuid "8c7bb5de-2e24-552b-9fb3-2501f210a725" :topic/math-academy-id 4149 :topic/title "The Inverse Function Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3abbc8c-d671-5959-b597-abe008d06807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453484} {:answer/id #uuid "0b13cfd9-8f9a-5bc4-b62e-9acf0c9835c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3abbc8c-d671-5959-b597-abe008d06807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453484} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e82a4ca-4e2a-5f53-9d73-7e8509121373" :answer-field/key "The function $f$ is invertible on $U.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454492} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c2343d7-3f2b-5c50-b87e-7d948c13e525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453486} {:answer/id #uuid "1f220f7b-6094-53ec-b07a-bbddab98f505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f220f7b-6094-53ec-b07a-bbddab98f505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453487} :answer-field/id #uuid "d93fb9b1-7a78-5650-bb54-3504271bf9eb" :answer-field/key "The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454493} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa16e892-8ac0-5080-820e-607b8aff0a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453488} {:answer/id #uuid "5b95beb1-056f-56f2-9817-32b180ee6f10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b95beb1-056f-56f2-9817-32b180ee6f10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453489} :answer-field/id #uuid "50770a0c-f153-535c-bc5d-43b6e01324e9" :answer-field/key "The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61853900-8f46-5757-9fa9-7e0c887a8b65" :question/math-academy-id "q-161849" :question/problem "Let $f:U\\to R$ be continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R$ such that $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U.$ Which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The inverse function theorem for single-variable functions states the following:\n\n*If $f:U\\to R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U⊆R,$ $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{′}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *${f}^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The function $f$ is invertible on $U.$” is false. According to the theorem, the function $f$ must be invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$ which could be smaller than $U.$ \n\nFor example, the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ satisfies the conditions of the inverse function theorem for $U=(0,\\pi )$ and $a=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ However, $f(x)$ is not invertible on the entire set $U,$ only on a subset of $U.$\n\n- Statement “The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$” is true. Indeed, the inverse ${f}^{-1}$ must be continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$\n\n- Statement “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$” is true. According to the theorem, we must have ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$”; “The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(b)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(a)}.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050540 :topic/id #uuid "521360f4-4398-5d66-ae61-73dcd0f74f49" :topic/math-academy-id 51 :topic/title "Power Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaa3babe-fc8a-5abc-bbf5-d3767d792f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453616} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e55f60-ad7a-5563-b5e2-159c439a70ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaa3babe-fc8a-5abc-bbf5-d3767d792f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453616} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7fdab7-f983-5bc2-bb04-1f895b807dfb" :answer-field/key "$P(∅)={∅,{∅}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de45af91-7568-5e47-b37f-4413eeae542d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453618} {:answer/id #uuid "710b6a64-0fde-520e-acb4-e44ce684997e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de45af91-7568-5e47-b37f-4413eeae542d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453618} :answer-field/id #uuid "c726e020-da13-5ea6-bafe-4ed894d72a26" :answer-field/key "$P({a,∅})={∅,{a},{a,∅}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1d878aa-3421-5025-86bd-8a47672bae55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453620} {:answer/id #uuid "84aca991-7429-5390-ab6f-fd636bcc8a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84aca991-7429-5390-ab6f-fd636bcc8a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453621} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd9eceba-08ff-5052-86b4-313736cb0156" :answer-field/key "$P({∅})={∅,{∅}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a540711c-ecf6-55f0-99c0-da5fdfa24e62" :question/math-academy-id "q-182224" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(∅)={∅,{∅}}$ is false. Notice that we are given the set $∅.$ So, its power set must be ${∅}.$\n\n- Statement $P({a,∅})={∅,{a},{a,∅}}$ is false. Notice that we are given the set ${a,∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{a},{∅},{a,∅}}.$\n\n- Statement $P({∅})={∅,{∅}}$ is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${∅}$ is ${∅,{∅}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P({∅})={∅,{∅}}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054640 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4954fe5-f1fe-590a-9540-280a14606a49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050540 :topic/id #uuid "521360f4-4398-5d66-ae61-73dcd0f74f49" :topic/math-academy-id 51 :topic/title "Power Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb402d5a-0b37-5e84-8c9e-ca364c7becf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471215} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb577a0-cc5e-55cb-b4e9-fb72f6a4b441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb577a0-cc5e-55cb-b4e9-fb72f6a4b441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471216} :answer-field/id #uuid "92f35a68-0bb5-5963-b302-95e8635c49e3" :answer-field/key "$P(P({x}))={∅,{∅},{{x}},{∅,{x}}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb7d2846-5cae-5909-80f6-634c1e8c1bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471217} {:answer/id #uuid "451e793e-944e-54e2-b7ce-7dbe24c3c6a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb7d2846-5cae-5909-80f6-634c1e8c1bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471217} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3697cde-7282-50bb-a234-7ad409f21d0e" :answer-field/key "$P({{x}})={∅,{x}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0283c931-eaf7-508c-a296-9ede0b8ab47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471219} {:answer/id #uuid "dd7d6682-a379-5b3d-b0b9-2726d2b7420c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd7d6682-a379-5b3d-b0b9-2726d2b7420c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471220} :answer-field/id #uuid "17cd737d-4caf-54ba-9eeb-0b52a6df76e4" :answer-field/key "$P({x,∅})={∅,{x},{∅},{x,∅}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5d0c05d7-b425-5e33-a2de-62cbcada849e" :question/math-academy-id "q-182247" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(P({x}))={∅,{∅},{{x}},{∅,{x}}}$ is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${x}$ is ${∅,{x}}.$ Therefore, $P(P({x}))={∅,{∅},{{x}},{∅,{x}}}.$\n\n- Statement $P({{x}})={∅,{x}}$ is false. Notice that we are given the set ${{x}}.$ Then, the power set of the set ${{x}}$ is ${∅,{{x}}}.$ Therefore, $P({{x}})={∅,{{x}}}.$\n\n- Statement $P({x,∅})={∅,{x},{∅},{x,∅}}$ is true. Notice that we are given the set ${x,∅}.$ So, its power set must be ${∅,{x},{∅},{x,∅}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(P({x}))={∅,{∅},{{x}},{∅,{x}}}$; $P({x,∅})={∅,{x},{∅},{x,∅}}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3868de94-f40b-55e1-bdb2-a7150e6b6c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471311} {:answer/id #uuid "631e930d-695f-5af5-aab9-dd585c953e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "631e930d-695f-5af5-aab9-dd585c953e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471312} :answer-field/id #uuid "66365a99-0b60-58bb-94f2-ccec01ad35dc" :answer-field/key "$R⊆R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472161} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b15f1878-c363-590e-a18b-cef0bf952481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471313} {:answer/id #uuid "e1261589-bf12-56e1-ba17-0ecce5d607fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15f1878-c363-590e-a18b-cef0bf952481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471313} :answer-field/id #uuid "2578266a-3ab5-5ff5-8e6f-8c792ea992ef" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472162} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed69226c-011b-5b2e-b15f-abdaa112a0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471315} {:answer/id #uuid "25d82bff-bad4-53b1-a8f4-aac1a9c3dd94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed69226c-011b-5b2e-b15f-abdaa112a0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471315} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7610904-dd5b-5286-aa99-f44196a2d25e" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{2}\\in Z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "878c8bf5-19ec-5026-9004-ee961047a572" :question/math-academy-id "q-215831" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $\\sqrt{3}\\in R$, then $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}}.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is trivial?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overbrace{Q}^{\\text{Always true}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Statement $R⊆R$ is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate ${x}^{2}=0$, defined for $x\\in R,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement $\\frac{1}{2}\\in Z$ is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $R⊆R$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf9e4aa9-8e45-51b3-b3b8-086dc158a25a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471317} {:answer/id #uuid "1dec0be7-4806-59e3-98b0-14968d4a61d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf9e4aa9-8e45-51b3-b3b8-086dc158a25a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471317} :answer-field/id #uuid "848d2e24-735f-5301-9b27-a19033fd2df7" :answer-field/key "$n$ is even" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c955bf8-730b-5d76-a57b-8e87b63787ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471319} {:answer/id #uuid "ae2d9626-802f-5ad4-ba44-11f523f067d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae2d9626-802f-5ad4-ba44-11f523f067d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471320} :answer-field/id #uuid "f74f6912-6c8b-56fe-a2d2-b4e096630c6c" :answer-field/key "$1-{n}^{2}<2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c54f76f8-6e8d-5829-92cc-9f289a4f3310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471321} {:answer/id #uuid "6024c44b-1400-5ac4-821d-8a05f32542f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c54f76f8-6e8d-5829-92cc-9f289a4f3310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471321} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3b09fe-6ba9-5625-9ccb-be0c318bab25" :answer-field/key "$1<n<2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e845f2cc-dfb4-5e80-9c1e-ef0b2c43bf19" :question/math-academy-id "q-216029" :question/problem "Let $n\\in Z.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $\\frac{n}{2}\\in Z,$ then $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}}.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is trivial?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overbrace{Q}^{\\text{Always true}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Predicate “$n$ is even”, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $1-{n}^{2}<2$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate $1<n<2$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $1-{n}^{2}<2$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4fb3905-55df-5307-b742-1b5ee71becee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471323} {:answer/id #uuid "687a1f83-58ae-59c6-980d-748e61017f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "687a1f83-58ae-59c6-980d-748e61017f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471324} :answer-field/id #uuid "e83dfcb0-1487-55a7-8777-e4c33fed1869" :answer-field/key "$1-|x|\\in Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472167} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94dcd398-9bb3-5c23-96f9-4f66db4bc936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471325} {:answer/id #uuid "1f3f307c-9cc7-5489-9c08-b3829f93e87c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94dcd398-9bb3-5c23-96f9-4f66db4bc936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471325} :answer-field/id #uuid "e360c1f4-9aa4-5f8d-995e-c5dae8c3dccf" :answer-field/key "${2}^{-1}<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a60a4bc-ff1b-5642-b8ce-d94e871ade4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471327} {:answer/id #uuid "91c7bc32-ec83-550e-b184-be712e2fd199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a60a4bc-ff1b-5642-b8ce-d94e871ade4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471327} :answer-field/id #uuid "07987a83-6f45-5147-a121-27bc2d71e9c2" :answer-field/key "$x>1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7628b9b-2926-5b1b-a6ec-eba49d9a9a32" :question/math-academy-id "q-216030" :question/problem "Let $x\\in Q.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If ${x}^{-1}<1,$ then $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}}.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is trivial?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overbrace{Q}^{\\text{Always true}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Predicate $1-|x|\\in Q$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement ${2}^{-1}<0$ is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $x>1$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $1-|x|\\in Q$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45f828cb-c8b1-5da4-9711-15ace712dffa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Vacuous Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34a0c713-82a0-5e54-9195-49999007aaeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471329} {:answer/id #uuid "3bae32ae-2fcf-5066-b6d8-5261a2ca782c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34a0c713-82a0-5e54-9195-49999007aaeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471329} :answer-field/id #uuid "717c53c5-7f91-58f1-9901-986694b231d1" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{x}{5}\\in Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d835ee88-916c-51b8-930a-3f05b769c7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1759