\n\n$$\n\\overbrace{P}^{\\text{Always false}}⇒\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our antecedents in turn.\n\n- Predicate $\\frac{x}{5}\\in Q$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $x>0$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $|x|<-1$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $|x|<-1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45f828cb-c8b1-5da4-9711-15ace712dffa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Vacuous Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b39e76-bc8c-52a1-9ab4-8b53fc905cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471335} {:answer/id #uuid "cff96380-a1c0-587a-987e-3f2acfcaf2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30b39e76-bc8c-52a1-9ab4-8b53fc905cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471335} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e2c93d8-0870-5cf3-b105-7f99a6eb460c" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{5}\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97bca418-db97-5bac-b2db-02fcefe49965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471337} {:answer/id #uuid "29f98fe9-52bd-59fd-8edc-d7d75dee4b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29f98fe9-52bd-59fd-8edc-d7d75dee4b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471338} :answer-field/id #uuid "4096e8f7-5304-599d-ad95-c167b5f3267f" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{2}\\in Z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d431875-8e83-5eba-909d-822a0ec932c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471339} {:answer/id #uuid "772955b8-21e1-5817-8746-49e813d39f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d431875-8e83-5eba-909d-822a0ec932c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471339} :answer-field/id #uuid "a890f1e2-6f72-5c8e-a3de-abe895d3b730" :answer-field/key "${x}^{5}>1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a08b61dd-f4dd-592d-9272-a1584fed8eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-216045" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}},$ then ${x}^{2}+2x<-1.$ \n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is vacuous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *vacuous proof* if the antecedent is always false: \n\n$$\n\\overbrace{P}^{\\text{Always false}}⇒\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our antecedents in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\sqrt{5}\\in R$ is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement $\\sqrt{2}\\in Z$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate ${x}^{5}>1$, defined for $x\\in R,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\sqrt{2}\\in Z$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45f828cb-c8b1-5da4-9711-15ace712dffa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Vacuous Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7fc458-0426-5cb1-b0f0-1e31fe748ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471341} {:answer/id #uuid "47405ffc-cfec-5943-9bf9-2b89f47af34f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c7fc458-0426-5cb1-b0f0-1e31fe748ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471341} :answer-field/id #uuid "552f79a8-e7b3-522e-8b3d-7198b74bc8d0" :answer-field/key "$n+1>n$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472176} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bd9c434-2c4b-562c-839d-16f535749a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471343} {:answer/id #uuid "70dacb19-1349-50ce-91a6-ff0482a093eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1