rn.\n\n- Predicate $n+1>n$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $\\sqrt{n}\\in Q$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $0<n<1$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $0<n<1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45f828cb-c8b1-5da4-9711-15ace712dffa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Vacuous Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fecc96dc-05fb-5de3-b963-2e113cb27686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471347} {:answer/id #uuid "988fc342-37b6-508a-a091-ab91d627f455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fecc96dc-05fb-5de3-b963-2e113cb27686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471347} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d82d74d-0ab4-5e70-91b9-bd0c7a9dfd4e" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{5}\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472179} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56ea38e7-97ac-50c0-bc84-297846484eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471349} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec15986-de28-5b61-9ef3-660fdfc28027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ec15986-de28-5b61-9ef3-660fdfc28027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471350} :answer-field/id #uuid "83156ad6-d168-5f5b-8918-8e33d2fd4047" :answer-field/key "${cos}^{2}⁡x>1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02275a12-5617-5eb2-9242-5bc687d8d277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471351} {:answer/id #uuid "d631db6b-f2d6-5754-a083-e9aa1223bc28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02275a12-5617-5eb2-9242-5bc687d8d277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471351} :answer-field/id #uuid "8469f468-1ac0-5b75-a026-b521daf95dde" :answer-field/key "$3x+2>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba9ef88d-4295-592b-9071-b4477cb43227" :question/math-academy-id "q-216054" :question/problem "Let $x\\in Q.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}},$ then $|x+3|<8.$ \n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is vacuous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *vacuous proof* if the antecedent is always false: \n\n$$\n\\overbrace{P}^{\\text{Always false}}⇒\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our antecedents in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\sqrt{5}\\in R$ is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate ${cos}^{2}⁡x>1$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate $3x+2>0$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${cos}^{2}⁡x>1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229161 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "151add00-204f-5795-aff9-cceddc26b24b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Other Methods" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049575 :topic/id #uuid "01533816-c819-5cab-8910-7cf6afa63383" :topic/math-academy-id 6685 :topic/title "Stability of Numerical Methods"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ac012a3-2b7a-5fad-8266-cc29057d1a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471411} {:answer/id #uuid "abb54835-096e-58c4-9110-0c96b1602e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb54835-096e-58c4-9110-0c96b1602e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471412} :answer-field/id #uuid "baf6dcb7-aa48-5618-82dc-14ac46166291" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=0.1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472211} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b402935f-58a9-5752-addc-960e5ce215cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471413} {:answer/id #uuid "895c8e8e-e7d7-5a94-aafc-1059169056b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895c8e8e-e7d7-5a94-aafc-1059169056b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471414} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae7169b-c55d-542d-8b6e-fb38683fad9c" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=0.8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00902814-4c4b-5e69-95a4-aabb29cc9517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471415} {:answer/id #uuid "36f94c4d-bb31-5998-9936-bc54616e115a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36f94c4d-bb31-5998-9936-bc54616e115a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471416} :answer-field/id #uuid "847bc4cf-85e6-5570-86a1-1732fb6b1d8a" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=1.2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5c47e6e-a2a4-5e7d-b62c-f7e727ef436a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471417} {:answer/id #uuid "903f2c91-49ea-5190-8870-540dc5840c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "903f2c91-49ea-5190-8870-540dc5840c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471418} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f00f93a-d100-582b-98a8-1e7e4c8bdb03" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7019503-fd19-5657-a7e0-238936f56d67" :question/math-academy-id "q-334241" :question/problem "For which of the following values is the implicit Euler method stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the implicit Euler method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method \n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the implicit Euler method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the implicit Euler Method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.1)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.1}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.1}| \\\\  & =0.9090…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.8)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.8}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.8}| \\\\  & =0.5555…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.2)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+1.2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{2.2}| \\\\  & =0.4545…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(5)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+5}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{6}| \\\\  & =0.1666…<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\lambda Δx=0.1$; $\\lambda Δx=0.8$; $\\lambda Δx=1.2$; $\\lambda Δx=5$.\n\nNote that, since the implicit Euler method is absolutely stable, it is stable for all possible values of $\\lambda Δx.$" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/title "Mathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420497} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420518}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afc801de-03b7-502f-b9c8-f19f4c68fc4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471513} {:answer/id #uuid "d060c791-2f52-56d5-9762-68ee81769280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afc801de-03b7-502f-b9c8-f19f4c68fc4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471513} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd94be66-084d-5fce-b5ff-a5131094ef86" :answer-field/key "$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c94250df-12f2-5dc7-ba7b-ba54131eb6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471515} {:answer/id #uuid "72fb50ec-bc64-58c3-b893-ff534273bff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c94250df-12f2-5dc7-ba7b-ba54131eb6c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471515} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6938560-02d0-5f9a-a09a-35e64a6e9bfb" :answer-field/key "$h:[0,2\\pi ]\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "371b703a-485e-500b-ad22-68bbfb32b6ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471517} {:answer/id #uuid "9dadf837-5a5b-540d-9627-c3bf4d8d2d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dadf837-5a5b-540d-9627-c3bf4d8d2d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471518} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9f14765-3b28-5e65-a4be-cb003368e296" :answer-field/key "$f:Q\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c69759b-6bd0-5ee4-a581-0fdeb88d4d4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76241" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- “$g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{4}$” is *not*  an injection.  For example, $g(1)=1=g(-1),$ but $1\\ne -1.$\n\n- “$h:[0,2\\pi ]\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$” is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2\\pi ),$ but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$\n\n- “$f:Q\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$” is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {2}^{{x}_{1}} & ={2}^{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡({2}^{{x}_{1}}) & ={log}_{2}⁡({2}^{{x}_{2}}) \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f:Q\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a40aa1f8-3059-5f5c-b4f4-a4957bb527ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453958} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8a0314-af7a-533f-8842-eafbbfc3f11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa8a0314-af7a-533f-8842-eafbbfc3f11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453959} :answer-field/id #uuid "01c07248-5ea7-5a73-b9e1-aa1ef9790d17" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fa36298-c254-5ae7-9f57-6e21928b62aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453960} {:answer/id #uuid "3530d61c-a4fb-52d2-b8da-3ead200044aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fa36298-c254-5ae7-9f57-6e21928b62aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453960} :answer-field/id #uuid "17ba2f9a-6d44-522e-9646-4c379db01776" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eeae9ef8-5d24-5c8a-bb5d-85d9ffc8052b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453962} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac8ebfc-3801-5252-b2b8-555ad3e72b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeae9ef8-5d24-5c8a-bb5d-85d9ffc8052b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453962} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab404ed8-bd98-5c3f-aadf-e57c714907e0" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d499a969-2317-5182-b93d-3971b580fa67" :question/math-academy-id "q-76260" :question/problem "For the function $f:Q\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{3},$ which of the following  statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is true. Indeed\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}^{3} & ={x}_{2}^{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}_{1}^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{{x}_{2}^{3}} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. As a counterexample, choose $2\\in R.$ There is no number $x\\in Q$ such that $f(x)=2.$ The only number $x$ that satisfies ${x}^{3}=2$ is $x=\\sqrt[3]{2}\\notin Q.$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The function is an injection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f45ad8ed-5b6d-5e46-b337-02ab271013b3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections From Functions Given Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c41f62f5-7637-554e-b0a5-72527d31b936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471525} {:answer/id 