ctions From Functions Given Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37b3c2fa-7551-588d-840a-ea83119bad7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471537} {:answer/id #uuid "3af9aa2b-eec1-59ce-84b4-fa541009cc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3af9aa2b-eec1-59ce-84b4-fa541009cc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471538} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bf6dc1f-9e90-5ea0-8430-eee9938fdcb0" :answer-field/key "$f:{-1,0,1,2,3}\\to Z$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "568dd441-ff12-5cb4-a941-03db3434a690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471539} {:answer/id #uuid "555408a4-81e1-5e46-9ca8-a8d529e2895b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555408a4-81e1-5e46-9ca8-a8d529e2895b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471540} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d798e58-7318-5c19-a372-7d8523c57d8c" :answer-field/key "$g:{-2,-1,0,1,2}\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={2}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472275} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83bf7342-2b6a-5899-a8fc-35881b6c4eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471541} {:answer/id #uuid "00421a0b-282f-5c80-877c-17c18d034c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83bf7342-2b6a-5899-a8fc-35881b6c4eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471541} :answer-field/id #uuid "dba742dd-43f9-5f00-ac05-4fdcec6aa9de" :answer-field/key "$h:Z\\to {-1,1}$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\pi )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3065c9f8-73e6-55e4-8dcd-b18452c2889c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77465" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are injections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- “$f:{-1,0,1,2,3}\\to Z$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{3}$” is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}^{3} & ={x}_{2}^{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- “$g:{-2,-1,0,1,2}\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={2}^{x}$” is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ {2}^{{x}_{1}} & ={2}^{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- “$h:Z\\to {-1,1}$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\pi )$” is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(2),$ but $0\\ne 2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f:{-1,0,1,2,3}\\to Z$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{3}$”; “$g:{-2,-1,0,1,2}\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={2}^{x}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bdf655b-7255-571c-b31f-2c19ac4a0867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471543} {:answer/id #uuid "dda6b314-fc5b-57b2-b98f-ffedaeec6a99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bdf655b-7255-571c-b31f-2c19ac4a0867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471543} :answer-field/id #uuid "37168c2c-1edd-551c-a12f-be1dfd5b8555" :answer-field/key "$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=|x|$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f032c94d-990d-581b-95a4-96685fcb08af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471545} {:answer/id #uuid "75eed30c-564b-56b5-8b2b-619d84b6bdba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75eed30c-564b-56b5-8b2b-619d84b6bdba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471546} :answer-field/id #uuid "993d2604-9db3-5f22-8e3f-39b362eaf4ca" :answer-field/key "$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)=4(x-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c84c134-22db-5232-9a60-c3fa7e3a6d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471547} {:answer/id #uuid "d66c08b1-58cf-5699-b34c-3bb58cc74b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c84c134-22db-5232-9a60-c3fa7e3a6d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471547} :answer-field/id #uuid "99f443a7-6607-5284-b20c-ebbf85c40142" :answer-field/key "$h:Q\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93abda0d-dd4f-575f-bfb4-2c2551c6ca10" :question/math-academy-id "q-77821" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- “$f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=|x|$” is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. For example, there is no value $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-1.$\n\n- “$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)=4(x-2)$” is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in Q,$ we can choose an $x\\in Q$ such that $g(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =y \\\\ 4(x-2) & =y \\\\ x & =\\frac{y}{4}+2\\in Q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that, \n\n$$\ng(x)=g(\\frac{y}{4}+2)=4([\\frac{y}{4}+2]-2)=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ 4({x}_{1}-2) & =4({x}_{2}-2) \\\\ {x}_{1}-2 & ={x}_{2}-2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause $g$ is both surjective and injective, $g$ is bijective.\n\n- “$h:Q\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$” is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Remember that the range of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is $[-1,1].$ This means that \n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nSo,  for example, there is no value $x\\in Q$ such that $h(x)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)=4(x-2)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d651d58c-8505-5b88-9051-45a55fccbbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471567} {:answer/id #uuid "2084d778-f394-5120-a035-085334534098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2084d778-f394-5120-a035-085334534098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471568} :answer-field/id #uuid "104907a6-cdd1-5226-80af-9238e48719dd" :answer-field/key "$3$ is odd" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472289} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4b7c76e-4f1a-5a35-aaa7-113b98824a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471569} {:answer/id #uuid "c90a8158-3fa5-5544-8d1c-0590cb740f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7c76e-4f1a-5a35-aaa7-113b98824a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471569} :answer-field/id #uuid "589fa4b5-e0cb-50a2-b3be-bd03ef21925e" :answer-field/key "$4$ is odd" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f04a6ac-0317-5ec8-b5dd-387f9a8446f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471571} {:answer/id #uuid "83d71d17-2958-5621-b3bc-0a068a57dce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f04a6ac-0317-5ec8-b5dd-387f9a8446f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471571} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8267449-e179-58cb-88c0-3d4f6726b361" :answer-field/key "$n$ is odd" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6066c3ca-d4e8-51fc-956b-cd9926b46fbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-80083" :question/problem "Let $n\\in Z.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $2$ is even, then $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}}.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is trivial?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overbrace{Q}^{\\text{Always true}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Statement “$3$ is odd” is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “$4$ is odd” is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate “$n$ is odd”, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$3$ is odd” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c805415f-c87d-50c5-b668-948fc46bcc7e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e35510f-5d3e-5217-88fc-7c44b314e258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471597} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd50cb3-a32f-5f64-95e6-5ec9409e1b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfd50cb3-a32f-5f64-95e6-5ec9409e1b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471598} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d53e89a-0146-52f2-80e0-530a9e476cb7" :answer-field/key "$f(0)\\ne f(1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc42154a-22b3-5d68-b3c1-14f6e025d1d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471599} {:answer/id #uuid "43a66160-0632-5271-b8f0-43543689ba60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43a66160-0632-5271-b8f0-43543689ba60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471600} :answer-field/id #uuid "03657d20-80fb-5db1-9d34-cc49a3cfbfe3" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be073be-7f85-5018-8338-460d95a4183c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471601} {:answer/id #uuid "ed92598c-87ea-5585-b964-631e0c12952c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed92598c-87ea-5585-b964-631e0c12952c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471602} :answer-field/id #uuid "238ccfc6-a5a4-5348-aeeb-45850bb195e5" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4333b20-5791-5886-a0e1-73362bfffb70" :question/math-academy-id "q-80365" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c3caf194f47cbc3fe36f969442df48e0a133ddbf77a9177e2e5e96822463c8a4.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(0)\\ne f(1)$ is true. According to the diagram, we have $f(0)=9$ (we have an arrow $0\\in X$ to $9\\in Y$) and $f(1)=0$ (we have an arrow from $1\\in X$ to $0\\in Y$).\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(0)\\ne f(1)$; “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$”; “$f$ is an injection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c805415f-c87d-50c5-b668-948fc46bcc7e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8eb7ec3e-b066-53aa-967e-ca9cd6d0fe63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471603} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c2051a-3e96-5d61-baf4-fdb7c710c72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :a