,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false, $f$ is not an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(-1)=f(1)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cec6272-e3c1-5d79-8e5f-cb77ba066b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471615} {:answer/id #uuid "59363834-1ac9-5e0d-9623-b9bdf850fa57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cec6272-e3c1-5d79-8e5f-cb77ba066b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471615} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c8166f1-6fe1-57a1-9c84-1d90e80859df" :answer-field/key "$f(-2)\\ne f(1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f98ee01d-c506-56f5-b241-ee8d6979bf62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471617} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f29d7b-ddc2-512a-884a-f31bc704d36f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f98ee01d-c506-56f5-b241-ee8d6979bf62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471617} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e346a9-d793-5487-abe6-bdec0eca1c88" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ed9cbc2-9dea-5d6b-9553-cdf98fc3d93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471619} {:answer/id #uuid "691c6242-9f3b-57a5-9a92-094e02607d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ed9cbc2-9dea-5d6b-9553-cdf98fc3d93d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471619} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd29552-cf51-56f9-888e-09e014b8609f" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **one-to-one**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb0a5436-5069-574d-ac30-ea6987db593d" :question/math-academy-id "q-80376" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d81a4317d789968de29f34b42358d44e74c8bbe4717467a4c780beb633dc0d5.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ whose graph is shown above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-2)\\ne f(1)$ is false. According to the graph, we have $f(-2)=f(1)=-1.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false. Again, we have $f(-2)=f(1)$ but $-2\\ne 1.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **one-to-one**” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152196 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a347133c-5e5a-5dd2-89ef-bdd14245ee6b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3007f3c-e5d9-54ac-acb1-fed4d2df4b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454036} {:answer/id #uuid "24a7f90e-4c9f-5e9b-bcfa-dd14f93bf09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3007f3c-e5d9-54ac-acb1-fed4d2df4b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454036} :answer-field/id #uuid "55403f69-b0a5-5b52-8781-9406fcd48ea3" :answer-field/key "$f(-3)=f(0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76861d48-ff1a-57b6-a42d-3d2fd72ba212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454038} {:answer/id #uuid "45b76c31-a794-5780-9602-0a7c9868204b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45b76c31-a794-5780-9602-0a7c9868204b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454039} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52bd5c3-60b8-54c4-916e-f386fc023174" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ced0fb16-8404-5b66-b796-6c626b0afbdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454040} {:answer/id #uuid "23bf899e-b083-56f2-8bdd-325f6c57396f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23bf899e-b083-56f2-8bdd-325f6c57396f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454041} :answer-field/id #uuid "9568da31-5657-5c24-abdd-6d98e31cae5d" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **one-to-one**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b7872e3a-407b-5f7a-81c4-4f36c9894a9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80378" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=3-{x}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/44/44a0d65bb3fc4f090dc82acc36a5c4657acaf5f9c8b0b80fe0a2cc30a3ac61e2.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-3)=f(0)$ is false. We have $f(-3)=3-(-3)^{3}=30$ and $f(0)=3-{0}^{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $R$ that map to the same element in $R.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $R,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **one-to-one**” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true, $f$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$”; “$f$ is **one-to-one**” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6f8b72e-897c-5e0d-92c3-ac73a0f28a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454042} {:answer/id #uuid "a76df206-0026-5aaf-81c5-975f9295aec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a76df206-0026-5aaf-81c5-975f9295aec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454043} :answer-field/id #uuid "a059fc80-3508-58b8-90cd-44eaf28b2ce6" :answer-field/key "$f(-1)=f(0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "508bcc28-61d9-5a0b-a2d8-3396206b5312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454044} {:answer/id #uuid "4586401f-787c-5e65-b2da-5a61f7b41aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "508bcc28-61d9-5a0b-a2d8-3396206b5312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454044} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d51ad1e-feb1-5643-b5ea-276c808f8a3b" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,1],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14f9f25f-46eb-51ab-9f54-b52c158c6ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454046} {:answer/id #uuid "96f218d4-0928-5de2-b331-75fa2971a3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14f9f25f-46eb-51ab-9f54-b52c158c6ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454046} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f51fddc-87f3-5da4-be10-651497ab82ad" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **one-to-one**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d7f30a04-d85b-56f5-8c95-f8906883e6fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-80386" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,1]\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/a0/a0e70acd2c7844de100c5c0cb0f85480af17921308b23d505b7ea639ce4690b9.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(-1)=f(0)$ is true. We have $f(-1)=(-1)^{3}+(-1)^{2}=0$ and $f(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,1],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false. We have $f(-1)=f(0)$ but $-1\\ne 0.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,1],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **one-to-one**” is false. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,1],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(-1)=f(0)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152197 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c2db8c-670b-521b-8942-3b89f1e95d3f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Injections For Functions Whose Domain or Codomain Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051035 :topic/id #uuid "7c0a3263-cc36-57b6-839b-6ff5594cae61" :topic/math-academy-id 2678 :topic/title "Injections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6537425a-3a23-527c-9da5-df969a886b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471621} {:answer/id #uuid "70384b8d-3049-593c-bffc-f225d07ff798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70384b8d-3049-593c-bffc-f225d07ff798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471622} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1968b7-411d-5d23-b491-bba506874af9" :answer-field/key "$f(1)\\ne f(2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "620220df-3c93-5179-9f74-25ff459cd253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471623} {:answer/id #uuid "7d76c890-f63f-55f5-8bfb-96b40fc2d65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d76c890-f63f-55f5-8bfb-96b40fc2d65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471624} :answer-field/id #uuid "4aa74849-6ed3-5eb6-ace4-7fa1690bd44b" :answer-field/key "$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36719e80-3e96-5b3d-8c80-f87abb5ce103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471625} {:answer/id #uuid "62ce85e1-7d09-54c4-a2a7-9d8e38606dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62ce85e1-7d09-54c4-a2a7-9d8e38606dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471626} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b46a5ab-4a37-5bc8-a5b2-54d266daa89c" :answer-field/key "$f$ is **one-to-one**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5a04c07f-9732-5fba-9678-462e7c23fd4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80387" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[1,\\infty )\\to [0,\\infty )$ which is given by $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/ae/aeda30e69b9bc433e5f345822d4221e194981ce132a022f28632814376c5910e.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f(1)\\ne f(2)$ is true. We have $f(1)=(1-1)^{2}=0$ and $f(2)=(2-1)^{2}=1.$\n\n- Statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true. As we can see from the graph, it passes the horizontal line test, meaning that there are no two distinct elements within $[1,\\infty )$ that map to the same element in $[0,\\infty ).$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “$f$ is **one-to-one**” is true. Indeed, since statement “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$” is true, $f$ is an injection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(1)\\ne f(2)$; “$∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [1,\\infty ),$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$”; “$f$ is **one-to-one**”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de15b416-0988-5682-8b4c-df22f0bdeba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471705} {:answer/id #uuid "bed38b8f-cd64-5808-97db-78c92453dfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de15b416-0988-5682-8b4c-df22f0bdeba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471705} :answer-field/id #uuid "12862809-b36b-5719-ad7e-aab5ef076094" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "636183c1-9b92-5010-925f-bf2aeb0bf21f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471707} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7e8dc-e348-599b-9e93-a55b371e6734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7e8dc-e348-599b-9e93-a55b371e6734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471708} :answer-field/id #uuid "e96b1a9f-58a9-5646-8df6-c11742da070a" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61e2d736-eecc-5dde-8872-cf1f75f92c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471709} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5391a9-7a0c-59b9-9fa7-c293bd935ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61e2d736-eecc-5dde-8872-cf1f75f92c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471709} :answer-field/id #uuid "f35689a1-265b-5ad7-8923-1155ca2a938d" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e966053-1b79-5d5f-9b9a-6962c445b14d" :question/math-academy-id "q-82293" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd6de23e9b33d0e86a91eb4bf6b81a9d443c1b389182f1c05bf10d048f0c0402.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. Consider $y=5.$ As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $5\\in Y.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* a surjection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a bijection” is false. Indeed, since statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false,  $f$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is an injection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6d0460-ea06-5cf0-9d95-66d1