r/id #uuid "eec2d395-740a-5cef-ac04-a21b8cf7a684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471716} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd2f7d7-d32f-52ad-b157-23fafe6b4b6d" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3819ae9-243b-5030-9bcc-f473557d3d03" :question/math-academy-id "q-82297" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bbe19e6a595d7b48e7f18382ed0a66452ba28c86925edad81a296cb7dd26a77f.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is true. Indeed, according to the diagram, for every element $y\\in Y,$ we have an arrow from some element $x\\in X$ to it, which means that $f(x)=y.$ So, $f$ is a surjection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a bijection” is true. Indeed, since both statements “$f$ is a surjection” and “$f$ is an injection” are true, $f$ is a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f$ is a surjection”; “$f$ is an injection”; “$f$ is a bijection”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152262 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22bcdfb2-485a-5242-a5b5-dd9ef8cee027" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined as Mapping Diagrams" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f5a15ef-9aac-5edc-8478-bfff007cdfd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471717} {:answer/id #uuid "8322b784-b416-5f2c-bfb8-2580815fc7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f5a15ef-9aac-5edc-8478-bfff007cdfd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471717} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca609a76-06c8-52db-8581-bd5c3848e1f6" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aee82d31-5b7a-5582-a21b-2fa920919744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471719} {:answer/id #uuid "3b0099d8-c719-5963-a690-03e8e902693a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aee82d31-5b7a-5582-a21b-2fa920919744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471719} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c020536-4c05-52fe-a219-595565574cf0" :answer-field/key "$f$ is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5caacba0-5907-578d-8806-41c31bfd65ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471721} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6c6ef8-4b43-5a6a-ad55-0aa584b65ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5caacba0-5907-578d-8806-41c31bfd65ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471721} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7d9db8e-6447-574c-a155-456b3f1f55a7" :answer-field/key "$f$ is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da5d5f20-c614-5648-b2cd-38bf72010ec2" :question/math-academy-id "q-82314" :question/problem "![](images/12/126abe41ac185c082d8cc28628e2db4b2708dd84ba351718184d949ddf582d3c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false. Consider $y=2.$ As we can see from the diagram, there are no elements contained within $X$ that have an arrow to $2\\in Y.$ So, it's *not true* that for all $y$ contained within $Y,$ there exists some $x$ contained within $X$ such that $f(x)=y.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* a surjection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is an injection” is false. We have $f(1)=f(4)$ but $1\\ne 4.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is *not* an injection.\n\n- Statement “$f$ is a bijection” is false. Indeed, since statement “$f$ is a surjection” is false (as well as statement “$f$ is an injection”), $f$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8921441-1dc4-5449-aacb-e1ab5bc13f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471723} {:answer/id #uuid "623e141a-1cbf-55c1-8dbd-d594b76a28d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8921441-1dc4-5449-aacb-e1ab5bc13f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471723} :answer-field/id #uuid "577e30c4-9496-58ff-bd73-fb5da086efb0" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da7e484-02af-5597-b1fd-da3b8176ebd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471725} {:answer/id #uuid "27e78f90-3fd0-5f93-8b4a-141561c450e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3da7e484-02af-5597-b1fd-da3b8176ebd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471725} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffdb055f-fba7-53d5-b7b3-3316bc59ab59" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472368} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3102ac0-d1e5-5474-bfac-ad06557b03a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471727} {:answer/id #uuid "195ad897-7a48-5a52-a5b1-f9353b04ade4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3102ac0-d1e5-5474-bfac-ad06557b03a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471727} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfaefc0f-ab90-5d24-983f-2d76b9e850dd" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24770296-d90b-538e-85f2-59d06d26123a" :question/math-academy-id "q-82317" :question/problem "For the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ which of the following  statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. For instance, $f(0)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )=f(2\\pi )$, but $0\\ne 2\\pi .$ So, $f(x)$ is not an injection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. For example, there is no $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=2.$ So, $f(x)$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152263 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfbebc20-1b48-5718-a057-b743c8af8de1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Defined on the Set of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bfbaec4-002f-56da-b603-ecb64b489280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471729} {:answer/id #uuid "ad13d9ab-3383-5fe3-ad9c-1c106572bb65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bfbaec4-002f-56da-b603-ecb64b489280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471729} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc29d875-c71c-520b-b763-2a953d8a8bac" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472370} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9720022a-1f68-56cc-99ed-1f884d93030f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471731} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7bbe52-574b-5d7b-b291-b264d3610735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9720022a-1f68-56cc-99ed-1f884d93030f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471731} :answer-field/id #uuid "4693e8e4-9ee4-5e25-ba31-16678f9c6ee2" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89adc61c-65db-5b4b-9356-e7f091e14040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471733} {:answer/id #uuid "1d8082f6-172b-5106-960f-2a9e83d9c98b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89adc61c-65db-5b4b-9356-e7f091e14040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471733} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e3ba47-0ae4-55b9-8bcb-8639b038f4be" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3380502f-56f6-501e-b560-ed1186ab069f" :question/math-academy-id "q-82324" :question/problem "For the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{2}-1,$ which of the following  statements are true? \n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is false. For instance, $f(-1)=0=f(1)$, but $-1\\ne 1.$ So, $f(x)$ is not an injection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. For example, there is no $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-2.$ So, $f(x)$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152265 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f237343d-2f8a-5a9f-9e5f-c9f22784547a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Functions Defined Algebraically" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1d22ff0-d65c-5ada-a9d6-2abf4c5625a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454072} {:answer/id #uuid "b2994bfa-b394-5f16-8b51-2743837eba99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2994bfa-b394-5f16-8b51-2743837eba99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454073} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e3a7e2c-6095-532e-9df6-ac3844ce7b49" :answer-field/key "The function is an injection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454786} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01a3361-56d5-5718-91e2-901eda2487c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454074} {:answer/id #uuid "1c8fcb79-82e9-5077-ab31-8f8bde4e1a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d01a3361-56d5-5718-91e2-901eda2487c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454074} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c41118-b50a-5deb-a97a-8d1bc552bc67" :answer-field/key "The function is a surjection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49a8178b-e2ee-5b6a-aed8-c5441cf79aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454076} {:answer/id #uuid "e346a0cb-8c92-55fa-9bfc-a2e9318b2fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49a8178b-e2ee-5b6a-aed8-c5441cf79aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454076} :answer-field/id #uuid "86eb81be-6c39-5f8e-a2e3-95bfdafc0e2b" :answer-field/key "The function is a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fc152a7c-fa1b-52cf-a24e-e996a44c8d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-82325" :question/problem "For the function $f:Q\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x},$ which of the following  statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is an injection” is true. Indeed\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}_{1}} & =\\sqrt[3]{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {(\\sqrt[3]{{x}_{1}})}^{3} & ={(\\sqrt[3]{{x}_{2}})}^{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is a surjection” is false. As a counterexample, choose $\\sqrt{2}\\in R.$ There is no number $x\\in Q$ such that $f(x)=\\sqrt{2}.$ The only number $x$ that satisfies $\\sqrt[3]{x}=\\sqrt{2}$ is $x=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}\\notin Q.$ Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{8}}={({2}^{3/2})}^{1/3}={2}^{1/2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is a bijection” is false because the function is not a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The function is an injection” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385810 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152264 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12e21e5-0a96-5f87-9642-d63d23e0038a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bijections For Functions Whose Domains or Codomains Are Real Intervals" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048139 :topic/id #uuid "82869b1d-f321-5919-b531-5dbc3fc95c4d" :topic/math-academy-id 2679 :topic/title "Bijections"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fi